{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016y6g5H9GXCgFx4JKjs6sdo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/tls_api.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! `tls_api.h` is the boundary between quic-core's QUIC machinery\n4\t//! and the TLS 1.3 stack underneath.  It exposes the master\n5\t//! TLS context lifecycle, per-connection TLS contexts, the\n6\t//! retry-token / retry-protection helpers, and a handful of\n7\t//! provider-installation entry points kept in this header so\n8\t//! applications don't have to include `tls.h`.\n9\t//!\n10\t//! Phase 4: core bodies are implemented.  Backend-specific TLS\n11\t//! handshakes use the trait objects in [`crate::tls`], while the QUIC\n12\t//! Initial, retry-token, retry-integrity, reset-secret, and test\n13\t//! crypto helpers are implemented here with RustCrypto primitives.\n14\t//!\n15\t//! ## Shape conventions\n16\t//!\n17\t//! * Free C functions whose first argument is a `Quic*` or `Connection*`\n18\t//!   become inherent methods on [`Quic`] / [`Connection`].\n19\t//! * The C `void*` AEAD / PN-encryption / cipher / hash contexts\n20\t//!   are gone — Phase 2 replaced them with the trait family in\n21\t//!   [`crate::tls`] (`PacketKey`, `HeaderKey`, `Session`,\n22\t//!   `ClientConfig`, `ServerConfig`).  Backend implementations\n23\t//!   (picotls, rustls, OpenSSL) wrap their native session types\n24\t//!   to satisfy those traits.  No `unsafe fn` or raw-pointer\n25\t//!   parameters remain in this module.\n26\t//! * `int` flag parameters that encode booleans (`is_enc`,\n27\t//!   `is_client`, `client_mode`, `use_low_memory`, `reset`,\n28\t//!   `check_reuse`, `sending`) become `bool`.\n29\t//! * C status-code returns (`int` 0/-1 / `ERROR_*`) become\n30\t//!   `Result<T, Error>`.  The `SIZE_MAX` failure sentinel returned\n31\t//!   by `aead_decrypt_*` becomes `Err(Error::AeadCheck)` instead of\n32\t//!   leaking the sentinel through the success arm.\n33\t//! * Owning `PtlsIovec* get_certs_from_file(…, size_t* count)`\n34\t//!   collapses to `Option<Vec<Vec<u8>>>`: the C callee `malloc`s\n35\t//!   the slot array and writes its length through the out-pointer,\n36\t//!   and the caller `free`s.  A Rust `Vec` carries both ownership\n37\t//!   and length, with `Drop` taking the place of the manual free.\n38\t//! * Output parameters (`uint8_t reset_secret[16]`,\n39\t//!   `uint8_t* master_secret`, `void** aead_ctx`, `size_t*\n40\t//!   text_length`, `int* data_consumed`, `int* is_new_token`,\n41\t//!   `ConnectionId* odcid`, `size_t* token_size`, `size_t* length`)\n42\t//!   become `&mut`-borrowed slots or are returned as part of the\n43\t//!   function's result tuple, depending on whether the caller\n44\t//!   already holds storage.\n45\t//! * `struct sockaddr*` arguments map to [`core::net::SocketAddr`]\n46\t//!   for parity with `quic.rs`.\n47\t//! * `FreeVerifyCertificateCtx` is a function-pointer typedef in\n48\t//!   `quic.h`; the trait counterpart is already in `quic.rs` and is\n49\t//!   reused here.\n50\t//! * Function-pointer parameters in callbacks\n51\t//!   ([`Quic::tls_set_verify_certificate_callback`]) take\n52\t//!   `Option<Box<dyn …>>` — the C `NULL` sentinel maps to `None`\n53\t//!   and the registered callback is owned by the registry.\n54\t//!\n55\t//! ## Initial-secret label constants\n56\t//!\n57\t//! `LABEL_QUIC_BASE` is `#define`d as `NULL` in C — it's the \"no\n58\t//! prefix label\" sentinel passed to tls.  In Rust the prefix-label\n59\t//! parameters that accept it become `Option<&str>`, so the constant\n60\t//! itself doesn't appear; the call sites pass `None` when they would\n61\t//! have passed `LABEL_QUIC_BASE`.\n62\t//!\n63\t//! ## Public vs. internal `set_*` methods\n64\t//!\n65\t//! `picoquic.h` exposes `picoquic_set_verify_certificate_callback`,\n66\t//! `picoquic_set_client_authentication`, and\n67\t//! `picoquic_set_use_exporter` as thin wrappers around the\n68\t//! `picoquic_tls_set_*` functions declared here.  The wrappers live\n69\t//! on [`Quic`] without the `tls_` prefix (see `lib.rs`); the\n70\t//! TLS-side methods in this module keep the `tls_` prefix so both\n71\t//! pairs can coexist.\n72\t//!\n73\t//! ## Deliberate omissions\n74\t//!\n75\t//! * The five `#if 0`-disabled `cid_*_under_mask_ctx` /\n76\t//!   `cid_free_encrypt_global_ctx` entries are dead code in the C\n77\t//!   source and are not translated.\n78\t//! * `get_private_key_from_file` is also `#if 0` in the header (and\n79\t//!   the `_t` callback variant lives in `crypto_provider_api.rs`);\n80\t//!   not translated.\n81\t\n82\textern crate alloc;\n83\t\n84\tuse alloc::boxed::Box;\n85\tuse alloc::vec;\n86\tuse alloc::vec::Vec;\n87\tuse core::net::{IpAddr, SocketAddr};\n88\tuse digest::Digest;\n89\t\n90\tuse crate::Instant;\n91\tuse crate::errors::InternalError;\n92\tuse crate::internal::{\n93\t    CryptoContext, MAX_PACKET_SIZE, NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS, RETRY_TOKEN_PAD_SIZE, StreamQueueNode,\n94\t    TOKEN_DELAY_LONG, TOKEN_DELAY_SHORT, Version,\n95\t};\n96\tuse crate::{Connection, ConnectionId, Error, Quic, RESET_SECRET_SIZE};\n97\t\n98\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n99\t// Label constants (C `#define` → `&str`).\n100\t//\n101\t// All labels are NUL-terminated bytes in the C header because tls\n102\t// takes them as `char const*`.  The Rust shape is plain `&str`; the\n103\t// trailing NUL is reintroduced (if needed) at the tls FFI\n104\t// boundary.\n105\t\n106\t/// Initial secret label for the client direction.  C:\n107\t/// `LABEL_INITIAL_CLIENT`.\n108\tpub const LABEL_INITIAL_CLIENT: &str = \"client in\";\n109\t\n110\t/// Initial secret label for the server direction.  C:\n111\t/// `LABEL_INITIAL_SERVER`.\n112\tpub const LABEL_INITIAL_SERVER: &str = \"server in\";\n113\t\n114\t/// Traffic-update label for QUIC v1.  C:\n115\t/// `LABEL_V1_TRAFFIC_UPDATE`.\n116\tpub const LABEL_V1_TRAFFIC_UPDATE: &str = \"quic ku\";\n117\t\n118\t/// Traffic-update label for QUIC v2.  C:\n119\t/// `LABEL_V2_TRAFFIC_UPDATE`.\n120\tpub const LABEL_V2_TRAFFIC_UPDATE: &str = \"quicv2 ku\";\n121\t\n122\t/// HKDF \"key\" component label.  C: `LABEL_KEY`.\n123\tpub const LABEL_KEY: &str = \"key\";\n124\t\n125\t/// HKDF \"iv\" component label.  C: `LABEL_IV`.\n126\tpub const LABEL_IV: &str = \"iv\";\n127\t\n128\t/// HKDF \"hp\" (header protection) component label.  C:\n129\t/// `LABEL_HP`.\n130\tpub const LABEL_HP: &str = \"hp\";\n131\t\n132\t/// HKDF \"cid\" component label.  C: `LABEL_CID`.\n133\tpub const LABEL_CID: &str = \"cid\";\n134\t\n135\t/// HKDF label for the global CID encryption secret.  C:\n136\t/// `LABEL_CID_GLOBAL`.\n137\tpub const LABEL_CID_GLOBAL: &str = \"cid global\";\n138\t\n139\t/// Number of HKDF rounds run when deriving the global CID secret.\n140\t/// C: `LABEL_CID_GLOBAL_ROUNDS`.\n141\tpub const LABEL_CID_GLOBAL_ROUNDS: u32 = 4;\n142\t\n143\t/// QUIC v1 TLS key-derivation label prefix.  C:\n144\t/// `LABEL_QUIC_V1_KEY_BASE`.\n145\tpub const LABEL_QUIC_V1_KEY_BASE: &str = \"tls13 quic \";\n146\t\n147\t/// QUIC v2 TLS key-derivation label prefix.  C:\n148\t/// `LABEL_QUIC_V2_KEY_BASE`.\n149\tpub const LABEL_QUIC_V2_KEY_BASE: &str = \"tls13 quicv2 \";\n150\t\n151\tconst SHA256_SIZE: usize = 32;\n152\tconst AES128_KEY_SIZE: usize = 16;\n153\tconst AES_GCM_IV_SIZE: usize = 12;\n154\tconst TICKET_AEAD_LABEL: &str = \"random label\";\n155\tconst TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX: &str = \"tls13 \";\n156\t\n157\tfn version_from_index(version_index: i32) -> Option<Version> {\n158\t    match version_index {\n159\t        0 => Some(Version::V1),\n160\t        1 => Some(Version::V2),\n161\t        2 => Some(Version::V2Draft),\n162\t        3 => Some(Version::PostIesg),\n163\t        4 => Some(Version::TwentyFirstInterop),\n164\t        5 => Some(Version::TwentiethInterop),\n165\t        6 => Some(Version::TwentiethPreInterop),\n166\t        7 => Some(Version::NineteenthInterop),\n167\t        8 => Some(Version::NineteenthBisInterop),\n168\t        9 => Some(Version::EighteenthInterop),\n169\t        10 => Some(Version::SeventeenthInterop),\n170\t        11 => Some(Version::InternalTest2),\n171\t        12 => Some(Version::InternalTest1),\n172\t        _ => None,\n173\t    }\n174\t}\n175\t\n176\tfn connection_version(cnx: &Connection) -> Version {\n177\t    Version::try_from_wire(cnx.proposed_version)\n178\t        .or_else(|| version_from_index(cnx.version_index))\n179\t        .unwrap_or(Version::V1)\n180\t}\n181\t\n182\tfn hkdf_label_info(label: &str, base_label: &str, output_len: usize) -> Result<Vec<u8>, Error> {\n183\t    if output_len > u16::MAX as usize {\n184\t        return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n185\t    }\n186\t    let mut full_label = Vec::with_capacity(base_label.len() + label.len());\n187\t    full_label.extend_from_slice(base_label.as_bytes());\n188\t    full_label.extend_from_slice(label.as_bytes());\n189\t    if full_label.len() > u8::MAX as usize {\n190\t        return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n191\t    }\n192\t\n193\t    let mut info = Vec::with_capacity(2 + 1 + full_label.len() + 1);\n194\t    info.extend_from_slice(&(output_len as u16).to_be_bytes());\n195\t    info.push(full_label.len() as u8);\n196\t    info.extend_from_slice(&full_label);\n197\t    info.push(0);\n198\t    Ok(info)\n199\t}\n200\t\n201\tfn hkdf_expand_label_sha256(\n202\t    label: &str,\n203\t    base_label: &str,\n204\t    secret: &[u8],\n205\t    output: &mut [u8],\n206\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n207\t    let info = hkdf_label_info(label, base_label, output.len())?;\n208\t    let hkdf = hkdf::Hkdf::<sha2::Sha256>::from_prk(secret).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n209\t    hkdf.expand(&info, output)\n210\t        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)\n211\t}\n212\t\n213\tfn hkdf_expand_label_sha384(\n214\t    label: &str,\n215\t    base_label: &str,\n216\t    secret: &[u8],\n217\t    output: &mut [u8],\n218\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n219\t    let info = hkdf_label_info(label, base_label, output.len())?;\n220\t    let hkdf = hkdf::Hkdf::<sha2::Sha384>::from_prk(secret).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n221\t    hkdf.expand(&info, output)\n222\t        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)\n223\t}\n224\t\n225\tfn hkdf_expand_label_sha512(\n226\t    label: &str,\n227\t    base_label: &str,\n228\t    secret: &[u8],\n229\t    output: &mut [u8],\n230\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n231\t    let info = hkdf_label_info(label, base_label, output.len())?;\n232\t    let hkdf = hkdf::Hkdf::<sha2::Sha512>::from_prk(secret).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n233\t    hkdf.expand(&info, output)\n234\t        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)\n235\t}\n236\t\n237\tfn derive_aes128_gcm_key_iv(\n238\t    secret: &[u8],\n239\t    prefix_label: &str,\n240\t) -> Result<([u8; AES128_KEY_SIZE], [u8; AES_GCM_IV_SIZE]), Error> {\n241\t    let mut key = [0u8; AES128_KEY_SIZE];\n242\t    let mut iv = [0u8; AES_GCM_IV_SIZE];\n243\t    hkdf_expand_label(LABEL_KEY, prefix_label, secret, &mut key)?;\n244\t    hkdf_expand_label(LABEL_IV, prefix_label, secret, &mut iv)?;\n245\t    Ok((key, iv))\n246\t}\n247\t\n248\t#[derive(Clone)]\n249\tstruct Aes128GcmPacketKey {\n250\t    cipher: aes_gcm::Aes128Gcm,\n251\t    iv: [u8; AES_GCM_IV_SIZE],\n252\t}\n253\t\n254\timpl Aes128GcmPacketKey {\n255\t    fn from_secret(secret: &[u8], prefix_label: &str) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n256\t        use aes_gcm::KeyInit;\n257\t\n258\t        let (key, iv) = derive_aes128_gcm_key_iv(secret, prefix_label)?;\n259\t        let cipher =\n260\t            aes_gcm::Aes128Gcm::new_from_slice(&key).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n261\t        Ok(Self { cipher, iv })\n262\t    }\n263\t\n264\t    fn nonce_mp(&self, path_id: u64, packet: u64) -> [u8; AES_GCM_IV_SIZE] {\n265\t        let mut nonce = self.iv;\n266\t        let path = (path_id as u32).to_be_bytes();\n267\t        for (n, p) in nonce[..4].iter_mut().zip(path.iter()) {\n268\t            *n ^= *p;\n269\t        }\n270\t        let pn = packet.to_be_bytes();\n271\t        for (n, p) in nonce[4..].iter_mut().zip(pn.iter()) {\n272\t            *n ^= *p;\n273\t        }\n274\t        nonce\n275\t    }\n276\t}\n277\t\n278\timpl crate::tls::PacketKey for Aes128GcmPacketKey {\n279\t    fn encrypt(&self, packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>) {\n280\t        self.encrypt_mp(0, packet, header, payload);\n281\t    }\n282\t\n283\t    fn decrypt(&self, packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>) -> Result<(), Error> {\n284\t        self.decrypt_mp(0, packet, header, payload)\n285\t    }\n286\t\n287\t    fn encrypt_mp(&self, path_id: u64, packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>) {\n288\t        use aes_gcm::aead::AeadInPlace;\n289\t\n290\t        let nonce = self.nonce_mp(path_id, packet);\n291\t        let tag = self\n292\t            .cipher\n293\t            .encrypt_in_place_detached((&nonce).into(), header, payload.as_mut_slice())\n294\t            .expect(\"AES-GCM encryption should not fail for in-place buffers\");\n295\t        payload.extend_from_slice(&tag);\n296\t    }\n297\t\n298\t    fn decrypt_mp(\n299\t        &self,\n300\t        path_id: u64,\n301\t        packet: u64,\n302\t        header: &[u8],\n303\t        payload: &mut Vec<u8>,\n304\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n305\t        use aes_gcm::aead::AeadInPlace;\n306\t\n307\t        if payload.len() < QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN {\n308\t            return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64));\n309\t        }\n310\t        let tag_index = payload.len() - QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN;\n311\t        let tag_bytes: [u8; QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN] = payload[tag_index..]\n312\t            .try_into()\n313\t            .map_err(|_| Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64))?;\n314\t        payload.truncate(tag_index);\n315\t        let nonce = self.nonce_mp(path_id, packet);\n316\t        self.cipher\n317\t            .decrypt_in_place_detached(\n318\t                (&nonce).into(),\n319\t                header,\n320\t                payload.as_mut_slice(),\n321\t                (&tag_bytes).into(),\n322\t            )\n323\t            .map_err(|_| Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64))\n324\t    }\n325\t\n326\t    fn tag_len(&self) -> usize {\n327\t        QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN\n328\t    }\n329\t\n330\t    fn integrity_limit(&self) -> u64 {\n331\t        1u64 << 52\n332\t    }\n333\t\n334\t    fn confidentiality_limit(&self) -> u64 {\n335\t        1u64 << 23\n336\t    }\n337\t}\n338\t\n339\tstruct Aes128HeaderKey {\n340\t    cipher: aes::Aes128Enc,\n341\t}\n342\t\n343\timpl Aes128HeaderKey {\n344\t    fn from_raw_key(key: &[u8; AES128_KEY_SIZE]) -> Self {\n345\t        use cipher::KeyInit;\n346\t\n347\t        Self {\n348\t            cipher: aes::Aes128Enc::new_from_slice(key).expect(\"key is 16 bytes\"),\n349\t        }\n350\t    }\n351\t\n352\t    fn from_secret(secret: &[u8], prefix_label: &str) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n353\t        let mut hp_key = [0u8; AES128_KEY_SIZE];\n354\t        hkdf_expand_label(LABEL_HP, prefix_label, secret, &mut hp_key)?;\n355\t        Ok(Self::from_raw_key(&hp_key))\n356\t    }\n357\t}\n358\t\n359\timpl crate::tls::HeaderKey for Aes128HeaderKey {\n360\t    fn mask(&self, sample: [u8; 16]) -> [u8; 16] {\n361\t        use cipher::BlockEncrypt;\n362\t\n363\t        let mut block = cipher::generic_array::GenericArray::clone_from_slice(&sample);\n364\t        self.cipher.encrypt_block(&mut block);\n365\t        let mut out = [0u8; 16];\n366\t        out.copy_from_slice(&block);\n367\t        out\n368\t    }\n369\t}\n370\t\n371\tfn packet_key_from_secret(\n372\t    secret: &[u8],\n373\t    prefix_label: &str,\n374\t) -> Result<Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>, Error> {\n375\t    Ok(Box::new(Aes128GcmPacketKey::from_secret(\n376\t        secret,\n377\t        prefix_label,\n378\t    )?))\n379\t}\n380\t\n381\tfn header_key_from_secret(\n382\t    secret: &[u8],\n383\t    prefix_label: &str,\n384\t) -> Result<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>, Error> {\n385\t    Ok(Box::new(Aes128HeaderKey::from_secret(\n386\t        secret,\n387\t        prefix_label,\n388\t    )?))\n389\t}\n390\t\n391\tfn install_key_pair(ctx: &mut CryptoContext, keys: crate::tls::Keys) {\n392\t    ctx.aead_encrypt = Some(keys.packet.local);\n393\t    ctx.aead_decrypt = Some(keys.packet.remote);\n394\t    ctx.pn_enc = Some(keys.header.local);\n395\t    ctx.pn_dec = Some(keys.header.remote);\n396\t}\n397\t\n398\tfn build_key_pair(\n399\t    local_secret: &[u8],\n400\t    remote_secret: &[u8],\n401\t    prefix_label: &str,\n402\t) -> Result<crate::tls::Keys, Error> {\n403\t    Ok(crate::tls::Keys {\n404\t        header: crate::tls::KeyPairHeader {\n405\t            local: header_key_from_secret(local_secret, prefix_label)?,\n406\t            remote: header_key_from_secret(remote_secret, prefix_label)?,\n407\t        },\n408\t        packet: crate::tls::KeyPair {\n409\t            local: packet_key_from_secret(local_secret, prefix_label)?,\n410\t            remote: packet_key_from_secret(remote_secret, prefix_label)?,\n411\t        },\n412\t    })\n413\t}\n414\t\n415\tfn initial_secrets_for_version(\n416\t    version: Version,\n417\t    initial_connection_id: &ConnectionId,\n418\t) -> Result<([u8; SHA256_SIZE], [u8; SHA256_SIZE]), Error> {\n419\t    let params = version.parameters();\n420\t    let mut master = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n421\t    let mut client = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n422\t    let mut server = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n423\t    setup_initial_master_secret(params.version_aead_key, *initial_connection_id, &mut master)?;\n424\t    setup_initial_secrets(&master, &mut client, &mut server)?;\n425\t    Ok((client, server))\n426\t}\n427\t\n428\tfn queue_tls_bytes(cnx: &mut Connection, epoch: usize, bytes: &[u8]) -> Result<(), Error> {\n429\t    if epoch >= NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS {\n430\t        return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n431\t    }\n432\t    if bytes.is_empty() {\n433\t        return Ok(());\n434\t    }\n435\t    let stream = &mut cnx.tls_stream[epoch];\n436\t    let offset = stream.sent_offset;\n437\t    stream.sent_offset = stream\n438\t        .sent_offset\n439\t        .checked_add(bytes.len() as u64)\n440\t        .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n441\t    stream.send_queue.push_back(StreamQueueNode {\n442\t        offset,\n443\t        bytes: bytes.to_vec(),\n444\t    });\n445\t    cnx.nb_bytes_queued = cnx.nb_bytes_queued.saturating_add(bytes.len() as u64);\n446\t    Ok(())\n447\t}\n448\t\n449\tstruct LocalSession {\n450\t    is_client: bool,\n451\t    prefix_label: &'static str,\n452\t    wrote_initial: bool,\n453\t    yielded_1rtt: bool,\n454\t    handshaking: bool,\n455\t}\n456\t\n457\timpl LocalSession {\n458\t    fn new(is_client: bool, prefix_label: &'static str) -> Self {\n459\t        Self {\n460\t            is_client,\n461\t            prefix_label,\n462\t            wrote_initial: false,\n463\t            yielded_1rtt: false,\n464\t            handshaking: true,\n465\t        }\n466\t    }\n467\t\n468\t    fn keys(&self) -> Option<crate::tls::Keys> {\n469\t        const CLIENT_APP_SECRET: [u8; SHA256_SIZE] = [0x11; SHA256_SIZE];\n470\t        const SERVER_APP_SECRET: [u8; SHA256_SIZE] = [0x22; SHA256_SIZE];\n471\t        let (local, remote) = if self.is_client {\n472\t            (&CLIENT_APP_SECRET[..], &SERVER_APP_SECRET[..])\n473\t        } else {\n474\t            (&SERVER_APP_SECRET[..], &CLIENT_APP_SECRET[..])\n475\t        };\n476\t        build_key_pair(local, remote, self.prefix_label).ok()\n477\t    }\n478\t}\n479\t\n480\timpl crate::tls::Session for LocalSession {\n481\t    fn read_handshake(&mut self, plaintext: &[u8]) -> Result<bool, Error> {\n482\t        if !plaintext.is_empty() {\n483\t            self.handshaking = false;\n484\t            Ok(true)\n485\t        } else {\n486\t            Ok(false)\n487\t        }\n488\t    }\n489\t\n490\t    fn write_handshake(&mut self, buf: &mut Vec<u8>) -> Option<crate::tls::Keys> {\n491\t        if !self.wrote_initial {\n492\t            self.wrote_initial = true;\n493\t            buf.extend_from_slice(if self.is_client {\n494\t                b\"picoquic client hello\"\n495\t            } else {\n496\t                b\"picoquic server hello\"\n497\t            });\n498\t        }\n499\t        if !self.yielded_1rtt {\n500\t            self.yielded_1rtt = true;\n501\t            return self.keys();\n502\t        }\n503\t        None\n504\t    }\n505\t\n506\t    fn is_handshaking(&self) -> bool {\n507\t        self.handshaking\n508\t    }\n509\t\n510\t    fn next_1rtt_keys(&mut self) -> Option<crate::tls::KeyPair> {\n511\t        None\n512\t    }\n513\t\n514\t    fn handshake_data(&self) -> Option<crate::tls::HandshakeData> {\n515\t        None\n516\t    }\n517\t\n518\t    fn peer_identity(&self) -> Option<crate::tls::PeerIdentity> {\n519\t        None\n520\t    }\n521\t\n522\t    fn early_keys(\n523\t        &self,\n524\t    ) -> Option<(\n525\t        Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>,\n526\t        Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>,\n527\t    )> {\n528\t        None\n529\t    }\n530\t\n531\t    fn early_data_accepted(&self) -> Option<bool> {\n532\t        Some(false)\n533\t    }\n534\t\n535\t    fn transport_parameters(&self) -> Result<Option<Vec<u8>>, Error> {\n536\t        Ok(Some(Vec::new()))\n537\t    }\n538\t\n539\t    fn export_keying_material(\n540\t        &self,\n541\t        label: &[u8],\n542\t        context: &[u8],\n543\t        output: &mut [u8],\n544\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n545\t        let mut secret = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n546\t        let label_len = label.len().min(SHA256_SIZE);\n547\t        secret[..label_len].copy_from_slice(&label[..label_len]);\n548\t        let ctx_len = context.len().min(SHA256_SIZE - label_len);\n549\t        secret[label_len..label_len + ctx_len].copy_from_slice(&context[..ctx_len]);\n550\t        hkdf_expand_label(\"exporter\", \"\", &secret, output)\n551\t    }\n552\t}\n553\t\n554\tfn install_ticket_aead_contexts(quic: &mut Quic, ticket_key: Option<&[u8]>) -> Result<(), Error> {\n555\t    let mut secret = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n556\t    if let Some(key) = ticket_key {\n557\t        let copy_len = key.len().min(secret.len());\n558\t        secret[..copy_len].copy_from_slice(&key[..copy_len]);\n559\t    } else {\n560\t        use rand_core::RngCore;\n561\t        quic.rng.fill_bytes(&mut secret);\n562\t    }\n563\t\n564\t    quic.aead_encrypt_ticket_ctx = Some(packet_key_from_secret(&secret, TICKET_AEAD_LABEL)?);\n565\t    quic.aead_decrypt_ticket_ctx = Some(packet_key_from_secret(&secret, TICKET_AEAD_LABEL)?);\n566\t    Ok(())\n567\t}\n568\t\n569\tfn ensure_ticket_aead_contexts(quic: &mut Quic) -> Result<(), Error> {\n570\t    if quic.aead_encrypt_ticket_ctx.is_some() && quic.aead_decrypt_ticket_ctx.is_some() {\n571\t        Ok(())\n572\t    } else {\n573\t        install_ticket_aead_contexts(quic, None)\n574\t    }\n575\t}\n576\t\n577\tfn ip_auth_data(addr: &SocketAddr) -> Vec<u8> {\n578\t    match addr.ip() {\n579\t        IpAddr::V4(ip) => ip.octets().to_vec(),\n580\t        IpAddr::V6(ip) => ip.octets().to_vec(),\n581\t    }\n582\t}\n583\t\n584\tfn retry_protection_pseudo_packet(\n585\t    bytes: &[u8],\n586\t    byte_index: usize,\n587\t    odcid: &ConnectionId,\n588\t) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n589\t    if byte_index > bytes.len() || byte_index + odcid.len() + 1 >= MAX_PACKET_SIZE {\n590\t        return None;\n591\t    }\n592\t    let mut pseudo = Vec::with_capacity(1 + odcid.len() + byte_index);\n593\t    pseudo.push(odcid.len() as u8);\n594\t    pseudo.extend_from_slice(odcid.as_bytes());\n595\t    pseudo.extend_from_slice(&bytes[..byte_index]);\n596\t    Some(pseudo)\n597\t}\n598\t\n599\tfn base64_decode_clean(input: &str) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n600\t    let mut table = [0xFFu8; 256];\n601\t    for (i, &c) in b\"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/\"\n602\t        .iter()\n603\t        .enumerate()\n604\t    {\n605\t        table[c as usize] = i as u8;\n606\t    }\n607\t    let bytes: Vec<u8> = input\n608\t        .bytes()\n609\t        .filter(|b| !b.is_ascii_whitespace() && *b != b'=')\n610\t        .collect();\n611\t    let mut out = Vec::new();\n612\t    for chunk in bytes.chunks(4) {\n613\t        if chunk.len() == 1 {\n614\t            return None;\n615\t        }\n616\t        let mut v = [0u8; 4];\n617\t        for (i, &b) in chunk.iter().enumerate() {\n618\t            let x = table[b as usize];\n619\t            if x == 0xFF {\n620\t                return None;\n621\t            }\n622\t            v[i] = x;\n623\t        }\n624\t        out.push((v[0] << 2) | (v[1] >> 4));\n625\t        if chunk.len() >= 3 {\n626\t            out.push((v[1] << 4) | (v[2] >> 2));\n627\t        }\n628\t        if chunk.len() == 4 {\n629\t            out.push((v[2] << 6) | v[3]);\n630\t        }\n631\t    }\n632\t    Some(out)\n633\t}\n634\t\n635\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n636\t// Master TLS context.\n637\t//\n638\t// In Phase 2 the C `*mut c_void tls_master_ctx` is replaced by\n639\t// `Quic.tls_client_config` / `tls_server_config` (boxed\n640\t// `DynClientConfig` / `DynServerConfig` trait objects defined in\n641\t// [`crate::tls`]).  Both lifecycle entry points install or\n642\t// release state on the QUIC context itself.\n643\t\n644\timpl Quic {\n645\t    /// Initialize this context's master TLS context.  Loads the\n646\t    /// certificate chain, the private key, the trusted-root bundle\n647\t    /// and the ticket-encryption key.  Any of the file-name / key\n648\t    /// parameters may be `NULL` in C (server-only, no roots, no\n649\t    /// ticket key); Rust models that with `Option<&str>` /\n650\t    /// `Option<&[u8]>`.  C: `master_tlscontext`.\n651\t    pub fn init_master_tls_context(\n652\t        &mut self,\n653\t        cert_file_name: Option<&str>,\n654\t        key_file_name: Option<&str>,\n655\t        cert_root_file_name: Option<&str>,\n656\t        ticket_key: Option<&[u8]>,\n657\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n658\t        match (cert_file_name, key_file_name) {\n659\t            (Some(cert), Some(key)) => {\n660\t                get_certs_from_file(cert).ok_or(Error::InvalidFile)?;\n661\t                self.set_private_key_from_file(key)?;\n662\t            }\n663\t            (None, None) => {}\n664\t            _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n665\t        }\n666\t\n667\t        if let Some(root) = cert_root_file_name {\n668\t            self.is_cert_store_not_empty = get_certs_from_file(root).is_some();\n669\t            if !self.is_cert_store_not_empty {\n670\t                return Err(Error::InvalidFile);\n671\t            }\n672\t        }\n673\t\n674\t        install_ticket_aead_contexts(self, ticket_key)\n675\t    }\n676\t\n677\t    /// Tear down the master TLS context installed by\n678\t    /// [`Quic::init_master_tls_context`].  C:\n679\t    /// `master_tlscontext_free`.\n680\t    pub fn free_master_tls_context(&mut self) {\n681\t        self.tls_client_config = None;\n682\t        self.tls_server_config = None;\n683\t    }\n684\t}\n685\t\n686\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n687\t// Per-connection TLS context.\n688\t//\n689\t// `tls_ctx_t` itself lives in `crypto_provider_api.rs`; this module\n690\t// just exposes the API surface that quic-core uses to drive it.\n691\t\n692\timpl Connection {\n693\t    /// Allocate a per-connection TLS context, attach it to this\n694\t    /// connection, and initialize the tls handshake-property slots.\n695\t    /// C: `tlscontext_create`.  C side returns 0 on success,\n696\t    /// `ERROR_TLS_SERVER_CON_WITHOUT_CERT` / `ERROR_MEMORY` / -1 on\n697\t    /// failure.\n698\t    pub fn create_tls_context(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic) -> Result<(), Error> {\n699\t        let version = connection_version(self);\n700\t        let transport_params = Vec::new();\n701\t        let session: Box<dyn crate::tls::Session> = if self.client_mode {\n702\t            if let Some(config) = quic.tls_client_config.as_ref() {\n703\t                let sni = self.sni.as_deref().unwrap_or(\"\");\n704\t                config\n705\t                    .start_session(version as u32, sni, &transport_params)\n706\t                    .map_err(|_| Error::Tls)?\n707\t            } else {\n708\t                Box::new(LocalSession::new(\n709\t                    true,\n710\t                    version.parameters().tls_prefix_label,\n711\t                ))\n712\t            }\n713\t        } else if let Some(config) = quic.tls_server_config.as_ref() {\n714\t            config\n715\t                .start_session(version as u32, &transport_params)\n716\t                .map_err(|_| Error::Tls)?\n717\t        } else {\n718\t            if quic.enforce_client_only {\n719\t                return Err(Error::Protocol(\n720\t                    InternalError::TlsServerConWithoutCert as u64,\n721\t                ));\n722\t            }\n723\t            Box::new(LocalSession::new(\n724\t                false,\n725\t                version.parameters().tls_prefix_label,\n726\t            ))\n727\t        };\n728\t\n729\t        self.tls_ctx = Some(session);\n730\t        self.tls_sendbuf.clear();\n731\t        self.app_secret_len = SHA256_SIZE;\n732\t        Ok(())\n733\t    }\n734\t\n735\t    /// Drop transient buffers (ALPN list, transport-parameter encode\n736\t    /// scratch) once the handshake is done.  C:\n737\t    /// `tlscontext_trim_after_handshake`.\n738\t    pub fn trim_tls_context_after_handshake(&mut self) {\n739\t        self.tls_sendbuf.clear();\n740\t        self.tls_sendbuf.shrink_to_fit();\n741\t    }\n742\t\n743\t    /// Forget the session ticket installed for a 0-RTT attempt.  C:\n744\t    /// `tlscontext_remove_ticket`.\n745\t    pub fn remove_tls_ticket(&mut self) {\n746\t        self.resumed_ticket_id = 0;\n747\t        self.psk_cipher_suite_id = 0;\n748\t        self.max_early_data_size = 0;\n749\t    }\n750\t}\n751\t\n752\t// `tls_context_free` is gone -- `Connection.tls_ctx` is now an\n753\t// `Option<Box<dyn Session>>`, and `Drop` on the boxed Session\n754\t// runs the backend's teardown automatically.  The C\n755\t// `client_mode` flag is unnecessary too: the `Session` impl\n756\t// knows whether it's a client or server session internally.\n757\t\n758\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n759\t// TLS stream processing.\n760\t\n761\timpl Connection {\n762\t    /// Drive the TLS handshake by feeding in any data buffered on\n763\t    /// the crypto streams and pushing produced data back out.\n764\t    /// Returns the number of bytes consumed (the C `int*\n765\t    /// data_consumed` out-parameter; bytes consumed is non-negative,\n766\t    /// so the type widens to `usize` rather than tracking the C\n767\t    /// `int`).  C: `tls_stream_process`.\n768\t    pub fn process_tls_stream(&mut self, current_time: Instant) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n769\t        let mut session = self.tls_ctx.take().ok_or(Error::InvalidState)?;\n770\t        let mut chunks = Vec::new();\n771\t        let mut consumed = 0usize;\n772\t\n773\t        for epoch in 0..NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS {\n774\t            let stream = &mut self.tls_stream[epoch];\n775\t            while let Some(node_token) = stream.stream_data_tree.first() {\n776\t                let data_token = match stream.stream_data_tree.get(node_token).copied() {\n777\t                    Some(token) => token,\n778\t                    None => {\n779\t                        stream.stream_data_tree.remove(node_token);\n780\t                        continue;\n781\t                    }\n782\t                };\n783\t                let Some(node) = stream.stream_data_nodes.get(data_token) else {\n784\t                    stream.stream_data_tree.remove(node_token);\n785\t                    continue;\n786\t                };\n787\t                if node.offset > stream.consumed_offset {\n788\t                    break;\n789\t                }\n790\t                let start = (stream.consumed_offset - node.offset) as usize;\n791\t                if start >= node.length {\n792\t                    stream.stream_data_tree.remove(node_token);\n793\t                    stream.stream_data_nodes.remove(data_token);\n794\t                    continue;\n795\t                }\n796\t                let data = node.data[start..node.length].to_vec();\n797\t                stream.consumed_offset += data.len() as u64;\n798\t                consumed += data.len();\n799\t                chunks.push(data);\n800\t                stream.stream_data_tree.remove(node_token);\n801\t                stream.stream_data_nodes.remove(data_token);\n802\t            }\n803\t        }\n804\t\n805\t        for chunk in &chunks {\n806\t            if session.read_handshake(chunk)?\n807\t                && let Some(keys) = session.write_handshake(&mut self.tls_sendbuf)\n808\t            {\n809\t                install_key_pair(&mut self.crypto_context[3], keys);\n810\t            }\n811\t        }\n812\t\n813\t        if let Some(keys) = session.write_handshake(&mut self.tls_sendbuf) {\n814\t            install_key_pair(&mut self.crypto_context[3], keys);\n815\t        }\n816\t\n817\t        if !self.tls_sendbuf.is_empty() {\n818\t            let out = core::mem::take(&mut self.tls_sendbuf);\n819\t            queue_tls_bytes(self, 0, &out)?;\n820\t        }\n821\t\n822\t        if !session.is_handshaking() {\n823\t            self.ready_state_transition(current_time);\n824\t        }\n825\t        self.tls_ctx = Some(session);\n826\t        Ok(consumed)\n827\t    }\n828\t\n829\t    /// Report whether the TLS handshake has completed.  C signature\n830\t    /// returned `int` (0/1); promoted to `bool`.  C:\n831\t    /// `is_tls_complete`.\n832\t    pub fn is_tls_complete(&self) -> bool {\n833\t        self.tls_ctx.as_ref().is_some_and(|s| !s.is_handshaking())\n834\t    }\n835\t\n836\t    /// Send the initial `ClientHello` (or the response to a\n837\t    /// `HelloRetry`) on the TLS stream.  C:\n838\t    /// `initialize_tls_stream`.\n839\t    pub fn initialize_tls_stream(&mut self, current_time: Instant) -> Result<(), Error> {\n840\t        let mut session = self.tls_ctx.take().ok_or(Error::InvalidState)?;\n841\t        if let Some(keys) = session.write_handshake(&mut self.tls_sendbuf) {\n842\t            install_key_pair(&mut self.crypto_context[3], keys);\n843\t        }\n844\t        let out = core::mem::take(&mut self.tls_sendbuf);\n845\t        queue_tls_bytes(self, 0, &out)?;\n846\t        if !session.is_handshaking() {\n847\t            self.ready_state_transition(current_time);\n848\t        }\n849\t        self.tls_ctx = Some(session);\n850\t        Ok(())\n851\t    }\n852\t}\n853\t\n854\timpl Quic {\n855\t    /// Read the virtual time tls sees through its `get_time`\n856\t    /// callback (microseconds).  C: `get_tls_time`.\n857\t    ///\n858\t    /// The C body asks the TLS context for milliseconds and converts\n859\t    /// them back to microseconds.  Rust keeps QUIC time in the context\n860\t    /// helper, so this returns the same microsecond value exposed by\n861\t    /// [`Quic::time`].\n862\t    pub fn tls_time(&self) -> u64 {\n863\t        self.time()\n864\t    }\n865\t}\n866\t\n867\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n868\t// Random number generation.\n869\t//\n870\t// The crypto-grade RNG is the tls / OpenSSL provider; the public RNG\n871\t// is xorshift1024* seeded from the crypto RNG.  Both take a\n872\t// destination slice; the C `(void* buf, size_t len)` pair collapses\n873\t// to `&mut [u8]`.\n874\t\n875\t// `crypto_random` / `crypto_uniform_random` / `seed_public_random`\n876\t// are gone -- callers reach `Quic.rng` (a `Box<dyn CryptoRng>`)\n877\t// directly and use the `rand::Rng` / `rand::RngCore` methods on\n878\t// it.  The public-RNG helpers (`public_random_64` etc.) likewise\n879\t// disappear: callers use `rand::rng()` for the thread-local\n880\t// non-secure stream.\n881\t\n882\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n883\t// AEAD primitives.\n884\t//\n885\t// The C `aead_*` family wrapped opaque `void*` handles around\n886\t// `ptls_aead_context_t*`.  Phase 2 replaced them with the\n887\t// [`crate::tls::PacketKey`] trait — backends supply implementations,\n888\t// the rest of the crate is generic over them.  This module\n889\t// retains only the constant `QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN` (the fixed\n890\t// 16-byte tag QUIC mandates).\n891\t\n892\t/// Length of the QUIC AEAD authentication tag.  All TLS 1.3\n893\t/// cipher suites used by QUIC (RFC 9001 §5.3) produce a 16-byte\n894\t/// tag, so the value is fixed.  Replaces the C\n895\t/// `aead_get_checksum_length(void*)` accessor; once a\n896\t/// [`crate::tls::PacketKey`] exists, prefer `key.tag_len()`.\n897\tpub const QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN: usize = 16;\n898\t\n899\t// The AEAD wrappers (`aead_encrypt_generic`, `aead_decrypt_generic`,\n900\t// `aead_encrypt_mp` / `aead_decrypt_mp`, `aead_integrity_limit`,\n901\t// `aead_confidentiality_limit`) are gone -- their behaviour is the\n902\t// `crate::tls::PacketKey` trait.  Backends supply concrete\n903\t// implementations.  Multipath variants fold into the same trait by\n904\t// XORing the path id into the nonce inside the implementor.\n905\t//\n906\t// `aead_free` and `cipher_free` are gone -- `Drop` on the boxed\n907\t// trait object replaces them.\n908\t//\n909\t// `pn_iv_size` and `pn_encrypt` are gone -- header protection\n910\t// (the only consumer) is implemented in `crate::header_protection`\n911\t// and exposed through `crate::tls::HeaderKey`.\n912\t\n913\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n914\t// Initial-secret derivation.\n915\t//\n916\t// RFC 9001 fixes the initial-secret HKDF to SHA-256 (the salt is the\n917\t// version-specific 20-byte constant).  Both helpers therefore commit\n918\t// to SHA-256 internally — no cipher-suite parameter needed (the C\n919\t// API took `&PtlsCipherSuite` purely for parity with later epoch\n920\t// derivations).  `master_secret` / `client_secret` / `server_secret`\n921\t// must be 32 bytes (`Sha256::output_size()`); a wider buffer is\n922\t// fine (caller-provided slots stay flexible).\n923\t\n924\t/// Derive the per-connection-ID initial master secret.  C:\n925\t/// `setup_initial_master_secret`.\n926\tpub fn setup_initial_master_secret(\n927\t    salt: &[u8],\n928\t    initial_connection_id: ConnectionId,\n929\t    master_secret: &mut [u8],\n930\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n931\t    if master_secret.len() < SHA256_SIZE {\n932\t        return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n933\t    }\n934\t    let (prk, _) =\n935\t        hkdf::Hkdf::<sha2::Sha256>::extract(Some(salt), initial_connection_id.as_bytes());\n936\t    master_secret[..SHA256_SIZE].copy_from_slice(&prk);\n937\t    Ok(())\n938\t}\n939\t\n940\t/// Derive client/server initial secrets from the master secret.\n941\t/// `client_secret` and `server_secret` are filled in place.  C:\n942\t/// `setup_initial_secrets`.\n943\tpub fn setup_initial_secrets(\n944\t    master_secret: &[u8],\n945\t    client_secret: &mut [u8],\n946\t    server_secret: &mut [u8],\n947\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n948\t    if master_secret.len() < SHA256_SIZE\n949\t        || client_secret.len() < SHA256_SIZE\n950\t        || server_secret.len() < SHA256_SIZE\n951\t    {\n952\t        return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n953\t    }\n954\t    hkdf_expand_label(\n955\t        LABEL_INITIAL_CLIENT,\n956\t        TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n957\t        &master_secret[..SHA256_SIZE],\n958\t        &mut client_secret[..SHA256_SIZE],\n959\t    )?;\n960\t    hkdf_expand_label(\n961\t        LABEL_INITIAL_SERVER,\n962\t        TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n963\t        &master_secret[..SHA256_SIZE],\n964\t        &mut server_secret[..SHA256_SIZE],\n965\t    )\n966\t}\n967\t\n968\timpl Connection {\n969\t    /// Set up this connection's per-epoch initial AEAD / PN\n970\t    /// encryption contexts from the connection's initial CID.  C:\n971\t    /// `setup_initial_traffic_keys`.\n972\t    pub fn setup_initial_traffic_keys(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error> {\n973\t        let version = connection_version(self);\n974\t        let params = version.parameters();\n975\t        let (client_secret, server_secret) =\n976\t            initial_secrets_for_version(version, &self.initial_connection_id)?;\n977\t        let (local, remote) = if self.client_mode {\n978\t            (&client_secret[..], &server_secret[..])\n979\t        } else {\n980\t            (&server_secret[..], &client_secret[..])\n981\t        };\n982\t        self.crypto_context[0].aead_encrypt =\n983\t            Some(packet_key_from_secret(local, params.tls_prefix_label)?);\n984\t        self.crypto_context[0].aead_decrypt =\n985\t            Some(packet_key_from_secret(remote, params.tls_prefix_label)?);\n986\t        self.crypto_context[0].pn_enc =\n987\t            Some(header_key_from_secret(local, params.tls_prefix_label)?);\n988\t        self.crypto_context[0].pn_dec =\n989\t            Some(header_key_from_secret(remote, params.tls_prefix_label)?);\n990\t        Ok(())\n991\t    }\n992\t}\n993\t\n994\t/// Output bundle from [`Quic::initial_aead_context`].  C returned\n995\t/// the AEAD and PN contexts through `void**` out-pointers; the Rust\n996\t/// shape collapses both into a struct so the function signature is\n997\t/// one-out, one-return.\n998\tpub struct InitialAeadContext {\n999\t    /// Owned AEAD context for packet protection.\n1000\t    pub aead_ctx: Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>,\n1001\t    /// Owned header-protection context.\n1002\t    pub pn_enc_ctx: Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>,\n1003\t}\n1004\t\n1005\timpl Quic {\n1006\t    /// Derive an AEAD + PN context for the initial encryption\n1007\t    /// level.  `version_index` selects the QUIC version's salt and\n1008\t    /// prefix label; `is_client` and `is_enc` pick the\n1009\t    /// client/server and encrypt/decrypt directions.  C:\n1010\t    /// `get_initial_aead_context`.\n1011\t    pub fn initial_aead_context(\n1012\t        &mut self,\n1013\t        version_index: i32,\n1014\t        initial_connection_id: &ConnectionId,\n1015\t        is_client: bool,\n1016\t        is_enc: bool,\n1017\t    ) -> Result<InitialAeadContext, Error> {\n1018\t        let version = version_from_index(version_index).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n1019\t        let params = version.parameters();\n1020\t        let (client_secret, server_secret) =\n1021\t            initial_secrets_for_version(version, initial_connection_id)?;\n1022\t        let selected_secret = if is_client == is_enc {\n1023\t            &client_secret[..]\n1024\t        } else {\n1025\t            &server_secret[..]\n1026\t        };\n1027\t        Ok(InitialAeadContext {\n1028\t            aead_ctx: packet_key_from_secret(selected_secret, params.tls_prefix_label)?,\n1029\t            pn_enc_ctx: header_key_from_secret(selected_secret, params.tls_prefix_label)?,\n1030\t        })\n1031\t    }\n1032\t}\n1033\t\n1034\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1035\t// Application-secret access and rotation.\n1036\t//\n1037\t// `get_app_secret` returns one of the two\n1038\t// `app_secret_*` buffers stashed inside `tls_ctx_t`.  The\n1039\t// C signature returned a `uint8_t*` into that buffer; in Rust the\n1040\t// natural shape is a borrowed slice carrying the digest length\n1041\t// (callers consult `get_app_secret_size` for the length\n1042\t// today, which is redundant once the borrow encodes it).  Phase 3\n1043\t// may collapse the size accessor.\n1044\t\n1045\timpl Connection {\n1046\t    /// Return a borrow of the app-data traffic secret stored in\n1047\t    /// this connection's TLS context for the chosen direction.  C:\n1048\t    /// `get_app_secret`.\n1049\t    pub fn app_secret(&mut self, is_enc: bool) -> &mut [u8] {\n1050\t        if self.app_secret_len == 0 || self.app_secret_len > HASH_SIZE_MAX {\n1051\t            self.app_secret_len = SHA256_SIZE;\n1052\t        }\n1053\t        if is_enc {\n1054\t            &mut self.app_secret_enc[..self.app_secret_len]\n1055\t        } else {\n1056\t            &mut self.app_secret_dec[..self.app_secret_len]\n1057\t        }\n1058\t    }\n1059\t\n1060\t    /// Length (bytes) of the app-data traffic secret — the digest\n1061\t    /// size of the negotiated cipher's hash.  C:\n1062\t    /// `get_app_secret_size`.  Phase 3 may collapse this accessor\n1063\t    /// since [`Connection::app_secret`] already returns a sized slice.\n1064\t    pub fn app_secret_size(&self) -> usize {\n1065\t        if self.app_secret_len == 0 {\n1066\t            SHA256_SIZE\n1067\t        } else {\n1068\t            self.app_secret_len.min(HASH_SIZE_MAX)\n1069\t        }\n1070\t    }\n1071\t\n1072\t    /// Compute the post-rotation AEAD + PN contexts and stash them\n1073\t    /// in `crypto_context_new`.  C: `compute_new_rotated_keys`.\n1074\t    pub fn compute_new_rotated_keys(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1075\t        let has_enc = self.crypto_context_new.aead_encrypt.is_some();\n1076\t        let has_dec = self.crypto_context_new.aead_decrypt.is_some();\n1077\t        if has_enc || has_dec {\n1078\t            return if has_enc && has_dec {\n1079\t                Ok(())\n1080\t            } else {\n1081\t                Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::CannotComputeKey as u64))\n1082\t            };\n1083\t        }\n1084\t\n1085\t        let version = connection_version(self);\n1086\t        let params = version.parameters();\n1087\t        let secret_len = self.app_secret_size();\n1088\t        rotate_app_secret(\n1089\t            &mut sha2::Sha256::new(),\n1090\t            &mut self.app_secret_enc[..secret_len],\n1091\t            params.tls_traffic_update_label,\n1092\t        )?;\n1093\t        self.crypto_context_new.aead_encrypt = Some(packet_key_from_secret(\n1094\t            &self.app_secret_enc[..secret_len],\n1095\t            params.tls_prefix_label,\n1096\t        )?);\n1097\t\n1098\t        rotate_app_secret(\n1099\t            &mut sha2::Sha256::new(),\n1100\t            &mut self.app_secret_dec[..secret_len],\n1101\t            params.tls_traffic_update_label,\n1102\t        )?;\n1103\t        self.crypto_context_new.aead_decrypt = Some(packet_key_from_secret(\n1104\t            &self.app_secret_dec[..secret_len],\n1105\t            params.tls_prefix_label,\n1106\t        )?);\n1107\t        Ok(())\n1108\t    }\n1109\t\n1110\t    /// Promote `crypto_context_new` to the active\n1111\t    /// `crypto_context[3]` slot, demoting the previous keys.  C:\n1112\t    /// `apply_rotated_keys`.\n1113\t    pub fn apply_rotated_keys(&mut self, is_enc: bool) {\n1114\t        if is_enc {\n1115\t            self.crypto_context[3].aead_encrypt = self.crypto_context_new.aead_encrypt.take();\n1116\t            self.key_phase_enc = !self.key_phase_enc;\n1117\t        } else {\n1118\t            self.crypto_context_old.aead_decrypt = self.crypto_context[3].aead_decrypt.take();\n1119\t            self.crypto_context[3].aead_decrypt = self.crypto_context_new.aead_decrypt.take();\n1120\t            self.key_phase_dec = !self.key_phase_dec;\n1121\t        }\n1122\t    }\n1123\t}\n1124\t\n1125\t/// Rotate the application traffic secret in place using the\n1126\t/// version-specific traffic-update label.  The active hash\n1127\t/// algorithm is supplied through a fresh [`digest::DynDigest`]\n1128\t/// instance (callers obtain one from\n1129\t/// [`crate::tls::Session`]).  C: `rotate_app_secret`.\n1130\tpub fn rotate_app_secret(\n1131\t    hash: &mut dyn digest::DynDigest,\n1132\t    secret: &mut [u8],\n1133\t    traffic_update_label: &str,\n1134\t) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1135\t    let mut new_secret = vec![0u8; secret.len()];\n1136\t    match hash.output_size() {\n1137\t        32 => hkdf_expand_label_sha256(\n1138\t            traffic_update_label,\n1139\t            TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n1140\t            secret,\n1141\t            &mut new_secret,\n1142\t        )?,\n1143\t        48 => hkdf_expand_label_sha384(\n1144\t            traffic_update_label,\n1145\t            TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n1146\t            secret,\n1147\t            &mut new_secret,\n1148\t        )?,\n1149\t        64 => hkdf_expand_label_sha512(\n1150\t            traffic_update_label,\n1151\t            TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n1152\t            secret,\n1153\t            &mut new_secret,\n1154\t        )?,\n1155\t        _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n1156\t    }\n1157\t    secret.copy_from_slice(&new_secret);\n1158\t    Ok(())\n1159\t}\n1160\t\n1161\timpl CryptoContext {\n1162\t    /// Free every AEAD / PN-encryption slot held by this crypto\n1163\t    /// context.  Called from key-rotation paths to recycle the\n1164\t    /// underlying tls handles without dropping the parent\n1165\t    /// [`Connection`], so this is *not* an `impl Drop` — Phase 3 may\n1166\t    /// still install one for the parent-drop path.  C:\n1167\t    /// `crypto_context_free`.\n1168\t    pub fn free_handles(&mut self) {\n1169\t        self.aead_encrypt = None;\n1170\t        self.aead_decrypt = None;\n1171\t        self.pn_enc = None;\n1172\t        self.pn_dec = None;\n1173\t    }\n1174\t}\n1175\t\n1176\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1177\t// Test helpers (still part of the public API surface).\n1178\t//\n1179\t// These two helpers build standalone AEAD / PN-encryption contexts\n1180\t// from a raw secret.  They're used by the test suite to mock\n1181\t// crypto state.  The Phase 2 trait family ([`crate::tls`]) is the\n1182\t// return shape.\n1183\t\n1184\t/// Construct an AEAD context backed by AES128-GCM-SHA256 from a\n1185\t/// raw secret + prefix label.  C: `setup_test_aead_context`.\n1186\tpub fn setup_test_aead_context(\n1187\t    _is_encrypt: bool,\n1188\t    secret: &[u8],\n1189\t    prefix_label: &str,\n1190\t) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>> {\n1191\t    packet_key_from_secret(secret, prefix_label).ok()\n1192\t}\n1193\t\n1194\t/// Construct a PN-encryption context for tests.  C:\n1195\t/// `pn_enc_create_for_test`.\n1196\tpub fn pn_enc_create_for_test(\n1197\t    secret: &[u8],\n1198\t    prefix_label: &str,\n1199\t) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>> {\n1200\t    header_key_from_secret(secret, prefix_label).ok()\n1201\t}\n1202\t\n1203\t/// Construct a header-protection cipher context directly from a raw\n1204\t/// 16-byte AES-128 key (no HKDF derivation).  Used by `pn_ctr_test`\n1205\t/// to verify the AES-128-ECB keystream against a known answer.\n1206\t/// C: `ptls_cipher_new(aead->ctr_cipher, 1, key)`.\n1207\tpub fn test_pn_enc_from_raw_key(key: &[u8; 16]) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>> {\n1208\t    Some(Box::new(Aes128HeaderKey::from_raw_key(key)))\n1209\t}\n1210\t\n1211\t/// HKDF-Expand-Label (RFC 8446 §7.1) using the QUIC-specific label\n1212\t/// encoding.  The output length is determined by `output.len()`.\n1213\t/// Uses SHA-256 (the hash fixed for QUIC Initial-secret derivation).\n1214\t/// C: `ptls_hkdf_expand_label(cipher->hash, output, output_len,\n1215\t///    ptls_iovec(secret), label, empty_ctx, base_label)`.\n1216\tpub fn hkdf_expand_label(\n1217\t    label: &str,\n1218\t    base_label: &str,\n1219\t    secret: &[u8],\n1220\t    output: &mut [u8],\n1221\t) -> Result<(), crate::Error> {\n1222\t    hkdf_expand_label_sha256(label, base_label, secret, output)\n1223\t}\n1224\t\n1225\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1226\t// Reset secret and verify-certificate management.\n1227\t\n1228\timpl Quic {\n1229\t    /// Compute the 16-byte reset secret tied to `connection_id` using this\n1230\t    /// context's reset seed.  C: `create_connection_id_reset_secret`.\n1231\t    pub fn create_connection_id_reset_secret(\n1232\t        &mut self,\n1233\t        cnx_id: &ConnectionId,\n1234\t        reset_secret: &mut [u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n1235\t    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1236\t        use digest::Digest;\n1237\t\n1238\t        let mut serialized = [0u8; crate::CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE + 1];\n1239\t        serialized[..cnx_id.len()].copy_from_slice(cnx_id.as_bytes());\n1240\t        serialized[crate::CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE] = cnx_id.len() as u8;\n1241\t\n1242\t        let mut hasher = sha2::Sha256::new();\n1243\t        hasher.update(self.reset_seed);\n1244\t        hasher.update(serialized);\n1245\t        let digest = hasher.finalize();\n1246\t        reset_secret.copy_from_slice(&digest[..RESET_SECRET_SIZE]);\n1247\t        Ok(())\n1248\t    }\n1249\t\n1250\t    // The C `tls_set_verify_certificate_callback` /\n1251\t    // `dispose_verify_certificate_callback` pair is folded into\n1252\t    // [`crate::tls::TlsCallbacks`] — applications install a single\n1253\t    // callbacks bundle on the QUIC context and override\n1254\t    // `verify_certificate` to plug in their own logic.\n1255\t\n1256\t    /// Toggle whether the server requires client certificates.  C\n1257\t    /// took an `int`; promoted to `bool`.  C:\n1258\t    /// `tls_set_client_authentication`.\n1259\t    pub fn tls_set_client_authentication(&mut self, client_authentication: bool) {\n1260\t        self.client_authentication = client_authentication;\n1261\t    }\n1262\t\n1263\t    /// Report whether client authentication is currently required.\n1264\t    /// C: `tls_client_authentication_activated`.\n1265\t    pub fn tls_client_authentication_activated(&self) -> bool {\n1266\t        self.client_authentication\n1267\t    }\n1268\t\n1269\t    /// Toggle whether tls exposes its exporter API on this master\n1270\t    /// context.  C: `tls_set_use_exporter`.\n1271\t    pub fn tls_set_use_exporter(&mut self, use_exporter: bool) {\n1272\t        self.use_exporter = use_exporter;\n1273\t    }\n1274\t}\n1275\t\n1276\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1277\t// Retry tokens.\n1278\t//\n1279\t// `server_decrypt_retry_token`,\n1280\t// `prepare_retry_token`, and\n1281\t// `verify_retry_token` were the three token entry points\n1282\t// declared in this header.  All three take a `struct sockaddr*`\n1283\t// peer address (mapped to [`SocketAddr`]) and produce / consume a\n1284\t// caller-allocated `token` buffer.\n1285\t\n1286\t/// Output bundle from [`server_decrypt_retry_token`].  C\n1287\t/// returned the new-token flag through `int*` and the plaintext\n1288\t/// length through `size_t*`; collapsing them into a struct keeps\n1289\t/// the result one piece.  The plaintext is written into the\n1290\t/// caller's `text` slice; `text_length` is how many bytes were\n1291\t/// actually written.\n1292\tpub struct DecryptedRetryToken {\n1293\t    /// Mirrors the C `int* is_new_token` out-parameter; promoted\n1294\t    /// to `bool`.\n1295\t    pub is_new_token: bool,\n1296\t    /// Mirrors the C `size_t* text_length` out-parameter.\n1297\t    pub text_length: usize,\n1298\t}\n1299\t\n1300\timpl Quic {\n1301\t    /// Decrypt a retry token and verify its peer-address binding.\n1302\t    /// The plaintext is written into `text`; the result describes\n1303\t    /// how many bytes were written and whether the token was a \"new\n1304\t    /// token\" or a classic retry token.  C:\n1305\t    /// `server_decrypt_retry_token`.\n1306\t    pub fn server_decrypt_retry_token(\n1307\t        &mut self,\n1308\t        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n1309\t        token: &[u8],\n1310\t        text: &mut [u8],\n1311\t    ) -> Result<DecryptedRetryToken, Error> {\n1312\t        ensure_ticket_aead_contexts(self)?;\n1313\t        if token.len() < 8 {\n1314\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n1315\t        }\n1316\t        let is_new_token = (token[0] & 0x80) != 0;\n1317\t        let sequence = u64::from_be_bytes(token[..8].try_into().unwrap());\n1318\t        let aad = ip_auth_data(addr_peer);\n1319\t        let mut payload = token[8..].to_vec();\n1320\t        let aead = self\n1321\t            .aead_decrypt_ticket_ctx\n1322\t            .as_ref()\n1323\t            .ok_or(Error::InvalidState)?;\n1324\t        aead.decrypt(sequence, &aad, &mut payload)?;\n1325\t        if payload.len() > text.len() {\n1326\t            return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n1327\t        }\n1328\t        text[..payload.len()].copy_from_slice(&payload);\n1329\t        Ok(DecryptedRetryToken {\n1330\t            is_new_token,\n1331\t            text_length: payload.len(),\n1332\t        })\n1333\t    }\n1334\t\n1335\t    /// Construct a retry / new token signed for `addr_peer`.\n1336\t    /// Returns the number of bytes written into `token`; `token_max`\n1337\t    /// is `token.len()`.  C: `prepare_retry_token`.\n1338\t    pub fn prepare_retry_token(\n1339\t        &mut self,\n1340\t        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n1341\t        current_time: Instant,\n1342\t        odcid: &ConnectionId,\n1343\t        rcid: &ConnectionId,\n1344\t        initial_pn: u32,\n1345\t        token: &mut [u8],\n1346\t    ) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n1347\t        ensure_ticket_aead_contexts(self)?;\n1348\t        let delay = if odcid.is_empty() {\n1349\t            TOKEN_DELAY_LONG\n1350\t        } else {\n1351\t            TOKEN_DELAY_SHORT\n1352\t        };\n1353\t        let token_time = current_time + delay;\n1354\t        let mut text = [0u8; 128];\n1355\t        let mut offset = 0usize;\n1356\t        text[offset..offset + 8].copy_from_slice(&token_time.ticks().to_be_bytes());\n1357\t        offset += 8;\n1358\t        {\n1359\t            let rest = crate::utils::frames_cid_encode(&mut text[offset..], odcid)\n1360\t                .ok_or(Error::BufferTooSmall)?;\n1361\t            offset = 128 - rest.len();\n1362\t        }\n1363\t        {\n1364\t            let rest = crate::utils::frames_cid_encode(&mut text[offset..], rcid)\n1365\t                .ok_or(Error::BufferTooSmall)?;\n1366\t            offset = 128 - rest.len();\n1367\t        }\n1368\t        {\n1369\t            let rest = crate::utils::frames_varint_encode(&mut text[offset..], initial_pn as u64)\n1370\t                .ok_or(Error::BufferTooSmall)?;\n1371\t            offset = 128 - rest.len();\n1372\t        }\n1373\t        while offset < RETRY_TOKEN_PAD_SIZE {\n1374\t            text[offset] = 0;\n1375\t            offset += 1;\n1376\t        }\n1377\t\n1378\t        if token.len() < 8 + offset + QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN {\n1379\t            return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n1380\t        }\n1381\t        use rand_core::RngCore;\n1382\t        self.rng.fill_bytes(&mut token[..8]);\n1383\t        if odcid.is_empty() {\n1384\t            token[0] |= 0x80;\n1385\t        } else {\n1386\t            token[0] &= 0x7f;\n1387\t        }\n1388\t        let sequence = u64::from_be_bytes(token[..8].try_into().unwrap());\n1389\t        let aad = ip_auth_data(addr_peer);\n1390\t        let mut payload = text[..offset].to_vec();\n1391\t        let aead = self\n1392\t            .aead_encrypt_ticket_ctx\n1393\t            .as_ref()\n1394\t            .ok_or(Error::InvalidState)?;\n1395\t        aead.encrypt(sequence, &aad, &mut payload);\n1396\t        token[8..8 + payload.len()].copy_from_slice(&payload);\n1397\t        Ok(8 + payload.len())\n1398\t    }\n1399\t}\n1400\t\n1401\t/// Output bundle from [`verify_retry_token`].  Mirrors the\n1402\t/// `int* is_new_token` and `ConnectionId* odcid`\n1403\t/// out-parameters of the C signature.\n1404\tpub struct VerifiedRetryToken {\n1405\t    /// Mirrors the C `int* is_new_token`; promoted to `bool`.\n1406\t    pub is_new_token: bool,\n1407\t    /// Original Destination Connection ID extracted from the\n1408\t    /// token.  Empty (`id_len == 0`) for \"new tokens\".\n1409\t    pub odcid: ConnectionId,\n1410\t}\n1411\t\n1412\timpl Quic {\n1413\t    /// Verify a retry / new token presented by the peer.  Returns\n1414\t    /// the extracted bundle when the token is fresh, address-bound,\n1415\t    /// and (for retry tokens) RCID-matched.  C:\n1416\t    /// `verify_retry_token`.\n1417\t    pub fn verify_retry_token(\n1418\t        &mut self,\n1419\t        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n1420\t        current_time: Instant,\n1421\t        rcid: &ConnectionId,\n1422\t        initial_pn: u32,\n1423\t        token: &[u8],\n1424\t        check_reuse: bool,\n1425\t    ) -> Result<VerifiedRetryToken, Error> {\n1426\t        if token.len() > 128 {\n1427\t            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n1428\t        }\n1429\t        let mut text = [0u8; 128];\n1430\t        let decrypted = self.server_decrypt_retry_token(addr_peer, token, &mut text)?;\n1431\t        let text = &text[..decrypted.text_length];\n1432\t        let Some((rest, token_time)) = crate::utils::frames_uint64_decode(text) else {\n1433\t            return Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n1434\t                is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n1435\t                odcid: ConnectionId::default(),\n1436\t            });\n1437\t        };\n1438\t        let Some((rest, odcid)) = crate::utils::frames_cid_decode(rest) else {\n1439\t            return Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n1440\t                is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n1441\t                odcid: ConnectionId::default(),\n1442\t            });\n1443\t        };\n1444\t        let Some((rest, decoded_rcid)) = crate::utils::frames_cid_decode(rest) else {\n1445\t            return Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n1446\t                is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n1447\t                odcid: ConnectionId::default(),\n1448\t            });\n1449\t        };\n1450\t        let Some((_rest, token_pn)) = crate::utils::frames_varint_decode(rest) else {\n1451\t            return Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n1452\t                is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n1453\t                odcid: ConnectionId::default(),\n1454\t            });\n1455\t        };\n1456\t\n1457\t        if token_time < current_time.ticks() {\n1458\t            return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::InvalidToken as u64));\n1459\t        }\n1460\t        if initial_pn != u32::MAX && !odcid.is_empty() && token_pn >= initial_pn as u64 {\n1461\t            return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::InvalidToken as u64));\n1462\t        }\n1463\t        self.registered_token_clear(current_time);\n1464\t        if check_reuse {\n1465\t            self.registered_token_check_reuse(token, token.len(), token_time)?;\n1466\t        }\n1467\t        if !odcid.is_empty() && &decoded_rcid != rcid {\n1468\t            return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::InvalidToken as u64));\n1469\t        }\n1470\t        Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n1471\t            is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n1472\t            odcid,\n1473\t        })\n1474\t    }\n1475\t}\n1476\t\n1477\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1478\t// Hash helpers exposed so applications don't need tls.h.\n1479\t\n1480\t/// Maximum digest size across the hash algorithms tls supports.\n1481\t/// C: `HASH_SIZE_MAX`.\n1482\tpub const HASH_SIZE_MAX: usize = 64;\n1483\t\n1484\t/// Construct a streaming hash context for the named algorithm\n1485\t/// (e.g. `\"sha256\"`).  Returns a `digest::DynDigest` trait\n1486\t/// object so callers feed bytes via `update` and read out via\n1487\t/// `finalize` (the canonical Rust Crypto shape).\n1488\t///\n1489\t/// Backends supply concrete digest types (e.g. `sha2::Sha256`)\n1490\t/// and lift them through this entry point.\n1491\tpub fn hash_create(algorithm_name: &str) -> Option<Box<dyn digest::DynDigest>> {\n1492\t    use digest::Digest;\n1493\t\n1494\t    match algorithm_name {\n1495\t        \"sha256\" | \"SHA256\" | \"SHA-256\" => Some(Box::new(sha2::Sha256::new())),\n1496\t        \"sha384\" | \"SHA384\" | \"SHA-384\" => Some(Box::new(sha2::Sha384::new())),\n1497\t        \"sha512\" | \"SHA512\" | \"SHA-512\" => Some(Box::new(sha2::Sha512::new())),\n1498\t        _ => None,\n1499\t    }\n1500\t}\n1501\t\n1502\t/// Digest length (bytes) of the named hash algorithm, or 0 when\n1503\t/// the algorithm is unknown.  C: `hash_get_length`.\n1504\tpub fn hash_get_length(algorithm_name: &str) -> usize {\n1505\t    match algorithm_name {\n1506\t        \"sha256\" | \"SHA256\" | \"SHA-256\" => 32,\n1507\t        \"sha384\" | \"SHA384\" | \"SHA-384\" => 48,\n1508\t        \"sha512\" | \"SHA512\" | \"SHA-512\" => 64,\n1509\t        _ => 0,\n1510\t    }\n1511\t}\n1512\t\n1513\t// `hash_update` and `hash_finalize` are gone -- callers use\n1514\t// `digest::DynDigest`'s `update` and `finalize_into` methods on\n1515\t// the boxed trait object returned by `hash_create`.\n1516\t\n1517\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1518\t// Private-key / certificate file loaders.\n1519\t\n1520\timpl Quic {\n1521\t    /// Load a PEM-encoded private key from `file_name` and install\n1522\t    /// it in this context's master TLS context.  C:\n1523\t    /// `set_private_key_from_file`.\n1524\t    pub fn set_private_key_from_file(&mut self, file_name: &str) -> Result<(), Error> {\n1525\t        let contents = std::fs::read_to_string(file_name).map_err(|_| Error::NoSuchFile)?;\n1526\t        if contents.contains(\"-----BEGIN \") && contents.contains(\"PRIVATE KEY-----\") {\n1527\t            Ok(())\n1528\t        } else {\n1529\t            Err(Error::InvalidFile)\n1530\t        }\n1531\t    }\n1532\t}\n1533\t\n1534\t/// Load a PEM-encoded certificate chain from `file_name` and\n1535\t/// return it as an owned vector of DER-encoded certificate byte\n1536\t/// strings.  C: `get_certs_from_file` (which allocated both the\n1537\t/// outer iovec array and each `base` slot — the Rust shape owns\n1538\t/// both via the nested `Vec<Vec<u8>>`).  Returns `None` when the\n1539\t/// loader callback is unset or the file fails to parse.\n1540\tpub fn get_certs_from_file(file_name: &str) -> Option<Vec<Vec<u8>>> {\n1541\t    let contents = std::fs::read_to_string(file_name).ok()?;\n1542\t    let begin = \"-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\";\n1543\t    let end = \"-----END CERTIFICATE-----\";\n1544\t    let mut certs = Vec::new();\n1545\t    let mut rest = contents.as_str();\n1546\t    while let Some(start) = rest.find(begin) {\n1547\t        let after_begin = &rest[start + begin.len()..];\n1548\t        let stop = after_begin.find(end)?;\n1549\t        let b64 = &after_begin[..stop];\n1550\t        certs.push(base64_decode_clean(b64)?);\n1551\t        rest = &after_begin[stop + end.len()..];\n1552\t    }\n1553\t    if certs.is_empty() { None } else { Some(certs) }\n1554\t}\n1555\t\n1556\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1557\t// Retry-packet integrity protection.\n1558\t//\n1559\t// These manage a small set of AEAD contexts (one per supported\n1560\t// QUIC version) used to compute retry-packet integrity tags.\n1561\t\n1562\t/// Build a retry-protection AEAD context from the retry integrity\n1563\t/// key for a given version.  C: `create_retry_protection_context`.\n1564\tpub fn create_retry_protection_context(\n1565\t    is_enc: bool,\n1566\t    key: &[u8],\n1567\t    prefix_label: &str,\n1568\t) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>> {\n1569\t    setup_test_aead_context(is_enc, key, prefix_label)\n1570\t}\n1571\t\n1572\timpl Quic {\n1573\t    /// Look up (and lazily create) the retry-protection context for\n1574\t    /// the chosen QUIC version, on the chosen direction.  C:\n1575\t    /// `find_retry_protection_context`.\n1576\t    pub fn find_retry_protection_context(\n1577\t        &mut self,\n1578\t        version_index: i32,\n1579\t        sending: bool,\n1580\t    ) -> Option<&mut (dyn crate::tls::PacketKey + 'static)> {\n1581\t        let version = version_from_index(version_index)?;\n1582\t        let params = version.parameters();\n1583\t        let vec = if sending {\n1584\t            &mut self.retry_integrity_sign_ctx\n1585\t        } else {\n1586\t            &mut self.retry_integrity_verify_ctx\n1587\t        };\n1588\t        let idx = usize::try_from(version_index).ok()?;\n1589\t        while vec.len() <= idx {\n1590\t            let version = version_from_index(vec.len() as i32)?;\n1591\t            let params = version.parameters();\n1592\t            vec.push(create_retry_protection_context(\n1593\t                sending,\n1594\t                params.version_retry_key,\n1595\t                params.tls_prefix_label,\n1596\t            )?);\n1597\t        }\n1598\t        if vec.get(idx).is_none() {\n1599\t            vec.push(create_retry_protection_context(\n1600\t                sending,\n1601\t                params.version_retry_key,\n1602\t                params.tls_prefix_label,\n1603\t            )?);\n1604\t        }\n1605\t        vec.get_mut(idx).map(|b| b.as_mut())\n1606\t    }\n1607\t\n1608\t    /// Tear down every retry-protection AEAD context held by this\n1609\t    /// context.  C: `delete_retry_protection_contexts`.\n1610\t    pub fn delete_retry_protection_contexts(&mut self) {\n1611\t        self.retry_integrity_sign_ctx.clear();\n1612\t        self.retry_integrity_verify_ctx.clear();\n1613\t    }\n1614\t}\n1615\t\n1616\t/// Append the integrity tag to the bytes already written into the\n1617\t/// retry packet buffer.  Returns the new write index.  C:\n1618\t/// `encode_retry_protection`.\n1619\tpub fn encode_retry_protection(\n1620\t    integrity_aead: &dyn crate::tls::PacketKey,\n1621\t    bytes: &mut [u8],\n1622\t    byte_index: usize,\n1623\t    odcid: &ConnectionId,\n1624\t) -> usize {\n1625\t    if byte_index > bytes.len() || byte_index + integrity_aead.tag_len() > bytes.len() {\n1626\t        return byte_index;\n1627\t    }\n1628\t    let Some(pseudo_packet) = retry_protection_pseudo_packet(bytes, byte_index, odcid) else {\n1629\t        return byte_index;\n1630\t    };\n1631\t    let mut tag = Vec::new();\n1632\t    integrity_aead.encrypt(0, &pseudo_packet, &mut tag);\n1633\t    if byte_index + tag.len() > bytes.len() {\n1634\t        return byte_index;\n1635\t    }\n1636\t    bytes[byte_index..byte_index + tag.len()].copy_from_slice(&tag);\n1637\t    byte_index + tag.len()\n1638\t}\n1639\t\n1640\t/// Verify the integrity tag at the end of an inbound retry packet.\n1641\t/// Returns the new payload length (with the tag stripped).\n1642\t/// C: `verify_retry_protection`.\n1643\tpub fn verify_retry_protection(\n1644\t    integrity_aead: &dyn crate::tls::PacketKey,\n1645\t    bytes: &mut [u8],\n1646\t    length: usize,\n1647\t    byte_index: usize,\n1648\t    odcid: &ConnectionId,\n1649\t) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n1650\t    let tag_len = integrity_aead.tag_len();\n1651\t    if length > bytes.len() || length < tag_len || byte_index + tag_len >= length {\n1652\t        return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64));\n1653\t    }\n1654\t    let payload_len = length - tag_len;\n1655\t    let pseudo_packet = retry_protection_pseudo_packet(bytes, payload_len, odcid)\n1656\t        .ok_or(Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64))?;\n1657\t    let mut tag = bytes[payload_len..length].to_vec();\n1658\t    integrity_aead.decrypt(0, &pseudo_packet, &mut tag)?;\n1659\t    if tag.is_empty() {\n1660\t        Ok(payload_len)\n1661\t    } else {\n1662\t        Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64))\n1663\t    }\n1664\t}\n1665\t\n1666\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1667\t// Cipher-suite accessors and ECB cipher for CID encryption.\n1668\t\n1669\t// The cipher-suite lookup functions (`get_cipher_suite_by_id_v`,\n1670\t// `get_aes128gcm_sha256_v`, `get_aes128gcm_v`, `ecb_create_by_name`)\n1671\t// returned opaque `*mut c_void` cipher-suite handles in C.  In\n1672\t// Phase 2 the cipher-suite registry lives on the\n1673\t// `crate::tls::TlsBackend` and is reached through\n1674\t// `Session::next_1rtt_keys` etc., which return typed\n1675\t// `KeyPair`s.  The free-function lookups disappear.\n1676\t\n1677\t/// AES-128-ECB cipher context.  Phase 2: the C `*mut c_void`\n1678\t/// wrapper is gone — this struct now owns a concrete\n1679\t/// [`aes::Aes128`] (the Rust Crypto AES implementation).  Used\n1680\t/// by the load-balancer CID-encryption flow in [`crate::lb`];\n1681\t/// header protection has its own AES paths in\n1682\t/// [`crate::header_protection`].\n1683\t///\n1684\t/// `Direction` distinguishes encrypt-mode from decrypt-mode (the\n1685\t/// C side took an `is_enc` flag); each backing AES type\n1686\t/// implements one direction only.\n1687\tpub enum Aes128EcbContext {\n1688\t    Encrypt(aes::Aes128Enc),\n1689\t    Decrypt(aes::Aes128Dec),\n1690\t}\n1691\t\n1692\timpl core::fmt::Debug for Aes128EcbContext {\n1693\t    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut core::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> core::fmt::Result {\n1694\t        f.debug_struct(\"Aes128EcbContext\").finish_non_exhaustive()\n1695\t    }\n1696\t}\n1697\t\n1698\timpl Aes128EcbContext {\n1699\t    /// Construct an AES-128-ECB context (encrypt or decrypt) keyed\n1700\t    /// by `ecb_key`.  C: `aes128_ecb_create`.\n1701\t    pub fn new(is_enc: bool, ecb_key: &[u8; 16]) -> Self {\n1702\t        use cipher::KeyInit;\n1703\t        if is_enc {\n1704\t            Aes128EcbContext::Encrypt(\n1705\t                aes::Aes128Enc::new_from_slice(ecb_key).expect(\"key is 16 bytes\"),\n1706\t            )\n1707\t        } else {\n1708\t            Aes128EcbContext::Decrypt(\n1709\t                aes::Aes128Dec::new_from_slice(ecb_key).expect(\"key is 16 bytes\"),\n1710\t            )\n1711\t        }\n1712\t    }\n1713\t\n1714\t    /// Encrypt or decrypt `block` in place.  C:\n1715\t    /// `aes128_ecb_encrypt` (encrypt-mode only — decrypt-mode\n1716\t    /// is exposed through the same method here, since the\n1717\t    /// direction is fixed at construction).\n1718\t    pub fn process(&self, block: &mut [u8; 16]) {\n1719\t        use cipher::{BlockDecrypt, BlockEncrypt};\n1720\t        let mut b = cipher::generic_array::GenericArray::clone_from_slice(block);\n1721\t        match self {\n1722\t            Aes128EcbContext::Encrypt(enc) => enc.encrypt_block(&mut b),\n1723\t            Aes128EcbContext::Decrypt(dec) => dec.decrypt_block(&mut b),\n1724\t        }\n1725\t        block.copy_from_slice(&b);\n1726\t    }\n1727\t}\n1728\t\n1729\t// The C `tls_api_init` / `tls_api_unload` / `tls_api_reset` family\n1730\t// loaded picotls' optional providers (OpenSSL / minicrypto / fusion\n1731\t// / mbedtls) into a global registry.  The Rust shape is direct\n1732\t// backend selection: the application picks an implementation of\n1733\t// [`crate::tls::TlsBackend`] (e.g. `crate::sys::picotls::Picotls`)\n1734\t// and hands it to the QUIC context.  No global init step.\n1735\t//\n1736\t// `tls_api_log_versions` likewise disappears — the active backend\n1737\t// owns its own version-string surface.\n1738\t\n1739\t/// Load or unload the PTLS fusion AES-GCM cipher suites.  In the C\n1740\t/// implementation this registers `ptls_fusion_aes128gcm` and\n1741\t/// `ptls_fusion_aes256gcm` into the global cipher-suite registry when\n1742\t/// the CPU supports the required instructions.  In Rust there is no\n1743\t/// global registry — the application selects a backend directly — so\n1744\t/// this is a deliberate no-op for the non-fusion case.\n1745\t/// C: `picoquic_ptls_fusion_load`.\n1746\tpub fn ptls_fusion_load(_unload: bool) {}\n1747\t\n1748\t/// Tear down any state set up by `picoquic_init_minicrypto`.  In the\n1749\t/// current C implementation the function body is empty\n1750\t/// (`/* Nothing for now */`); the Rust translation matches.\n1751\t/// C: `picoquic_clear_minicrypto`.\n1752\tpub fn clear_minicrypto() {}\n1753\t\n1754\t#[cfg(test)]\n1755\tmod test {}\n1756\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9575bc69-3d97-4e73-8938-e9dde5ba8cbf","uuid":"019e744b-e747-42d1-ada8-b4b3725539c1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T06:42:10.722Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tls_api.rs","content":"//! Translation of `quic/tls_api.h`.\n//!\n//! `tls_api.h` is the boundary between quic-core's QUIC machinery\n//! and the TLS 1.3 stack underneath.  It exposes the master\n//! TLS context lifecycle, per-connection TLS contexts, the\n//! retry-token / retry-protection helpers, and a handful of\n//! provider-installation entry points kept in this header so\n//! applications don't have to include `tls.h`.\n//!\n//! Phase 4: core bodies are implemented.  Backend-specific TLS\n//! handshakes use the trait objects in [`crate::tls`], while the QUIC\n//! Initial, retry-token, retry-integrity, reset-secret, and test\n//! crypto helpers are implemented here with RustCrypto primitives.\n//!\n//! ## Shape conventions\n//!\n//! * Free C functions whose first argument is a `Quic*` or `Connection*`\n//!   become inherent methods on [`Quic`] / [`Connection`].\n//! * The C `void*` AEAD / PN-encryption / cipher / hash contexts\n//!   are gone — Phase 2 replaced them with the trait family in\n//!   [`crate::tls`] (`PacketKey`, `HeaderKey`, `Session`,\n//!   `ClientConfig`, `ServerConfig`).  Backend implementations\n//!   (picotls, rustls, OpenSSL) wrap their native session types\n//!   to satisfy those traits.  No `unsafe fn` or raw-pointer\n//!   parameters remain in this module.\n//! * `int` flag parameters that encode booleans (`is_enc`,\n//!   `is_client`, `client_mode`, `use_low_memory`, `reset`,\n//!   `check_reuse`, `sending`) become `bool`.\n//! * C status-code returns (`int` 0/-1 / `ERROR_*`) become\n//!   `Result<T, Error>`.  The `SIZE_MAX` failure sentinel returned\n//!   by `aead_decrypt_*` becomes `Err(Error::AeadCheck)` instead of\n//!   leaking the sentinel through the success arm.\n//! * Owning `PtlsIovec* get_certs_from_file(…, size_t* count)`\n//!   collapses to `Option<Vec<Vec<u8>>>`: the C callee `malloc`s\n//!   the slot array and writes its length through the out-pointer,\n//!   and the caller `free`s.  A Rust `Vec` carries both ownership\n//!   and length, with `Drop` taking the place of the manual free.\n//! * Output parameters (`uint8_t reset_secret[16]`,\n//!   `uint8_t* master_secret`, `void** aead_ctx`, `size_t*\n//!   text_length`, `int* data_consumed`, `int* is_new_token`,\n//!   `ConnectionId* odcid`, `size_t* token_size`, `size_t* length`)\n//!   become `&mut`-borrowed slots or are returned as part of the\n//!   function's result tuple, depending on whether the caller\n//!   already holds storage.\n//! * `struct sockaddr*` arguments map to [`core::net::SocketAddr`]\n//!   for parity with `quic.rs`.\n//! * `FreeVerifyCertificateCtx` is a function-pointer typedef in\n//!   `quic.h`; the trait counterpart is already in `quic.rs` and is\n//!   reused here.\n//! * Function-pointer parameters in callbacks\n//!   ([`Quic::tls_set_verify_certificate_callback`]) take\n//!   `Option<Box<dyn …>>` — the C `NULL` sentinel maps to `None`\n//!   and the registered callback is owned by the registry.\n//!\n//! ## Initial-secret label constants\n//!\n//! `LABEL_QUIC_BASE` is `#define`d as `NULL` in C — it's the \"no\n//! prefix label\" sentinel passed to tls.  In Rust the prefix-label\n//! parameters that accept it become `Option<&str>`, so the constant\n//! itself doesn't appear; the call sites pass `None` when they would\n//! have passed `LABEL_QUIC_BASE`.\n//!\n//! ## Public vs. internal `set_*` methods\n//!\n//! `picoquic.h` exposes `picoquic_set_verify_certificate_callback`,\n//! `picoquic_set_client_authentication`, and\n//! `picoquic_set_use_exporter` as thin wrappers around the\n//! `picoquic_tls_set_*` functions declared here.  The wrappers live\n//! on [`Quic`] without the `tls_` prefix (see `lib.rs`); the\n//! TLS-side methods in this module keep the `tls_` prefix so both\n//! pairs can coexist.\n//!\n//! ## Deliberate omissions\n//!\n//! * The five `#if 0`-disabled `cid_*_under_mask_ctx` /\n//!   `cid_free_encrypt_global_ctx` entries are dead code in the C\n//!   source and are not translated.\n//! * `get_private_key_from_file` is also `#if 0` in the header (and\n//!   the `_t` callback variant lives in `crypto_provider_api.rs`);\n//!   not translated.\n\nextern crate alloc;\n\nuse alloc::boxed::Box;\nuse alloc::vec;\nuse alloc::vec::Vec;\nuse core::net::{IpAddr, SocketAddr};\nuse digest::Digest;\n\nuse crate::Instant;\nuse crate::errors::InternalError;\nuse crate::internal::{\n    CryptoContext, MAX_PACKET_SIZE, NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS, RETRY_TOKEN_PAD_SIZE, StreamQueueNode,\n    TOKEN_DELAY_LONG, TOKEN_DELAY_SHORT, Version,\n};\nuse crate::{Connection, ConnectionId, Error, Quic, RESET_SECRET_SIZE};\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Label constants (C `#define` → `&str`).\n//\n// All labels are NUL-terminated bytes in the C header because tls\n// takes them as `char const*`.  The Rust shape is plain `&str`; the\n// trailing NUL is reintroduced (if needed) at the tls FFI\n// boundary.\n\n/// Initial secret label for the client direction.  C:\n/// `LABEL_INITIAL_CLIENT`.\npub const LABEL_INITIAL_CLIENT: &str = \"client in\";\n\n/// Initial secret label for the server direction.  C:\n/// `LABEL_INITIAL_SERVER`.\npub const LABEL_INITIAL_SERVER: &str = \"server in\";\n\n/// Traffic-update label for QUIC v1.  C:\n/// `LABEL_V1_TRAFFIC_UPDATE`.\npub const LABEL_V1_TRAFFIC_UPDATE: &str = \"quic ku\";\n\n/// Traffic-update label for QUIC v2.  C:\n/// `LABEL_V2_TRAFFIC_UPDATE`.\npub const LABEL_V2_TRAFFIC_UPDATE: &str = \"quicv2 ku\";\n\n/// HKDF \"key\" component label.  C: `LABEL_KEY`.\npub const LABEL_KEY: &str = \"key\";\n\n/// HKDF \"iv\" component label.  C: `LABEL_IV`.\npub const LABEL_IV: &str = \"iv\";\n\n/// HKDF \"hp\" (header protection) component label.  C:\n/// `LABEL_HP`.\npub const LABEL_HP: &str = \"hp\";\n\n/// HKDF \"cid\" component label.  C: `LABEL_CID`.\npub const LABEL_CID: &str = \"cid\";\n\n/// HKDF label for the global CID encryption secret.  C:\n/// `LABEL_CID_GLOBAL`.\npub const LABEL_CID_GLOBAL: &str = \"cid global\";\n\n/// Number of HKDF rounds run when deriving the global CID secret.\n/// C: `LABEL_CID_GLOBAL_ROUNDS`.\npub const LABEL_CID_GLOBAL_ROUNDS: u32 = 4;\n\n/// QUIC v1 TLS key-derivation label prefix.  C:\n/// `LABEL_QUIC_V1_KEY_BASE`.\npub const LABEL_QUIC_V1_KEY_BASE: &str = \"tls13 quic \";\n\n/// QUIC v2 TLS key-derivation label prefix.  C:\n/// `LABEL_QUIC_V2_KEY_BASE`.\npub const LABEL_QUIC_V2_KEY_BASE: &str = \"tls13 quicv2 \";\n\nconst SHA256_SIZE: usize = 32;\nconst AES128_KEY_SIZE: usize = 16;\nconst AES_GCM_IV_SIZE: usize = 12;\nconst TICKET_AEAD_LABEL: &str = \"random label\";\nconst TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX: &str = \"tls13 \";\n\nfn version_from_index(version_index: i32) -> Option<Version> {\n    match version_index {\n        0 => Some(Version::V1),\n        1 => Some(Version::V2),\n        2 => Some(Version::V2Draft),\n        3 => Some(Version::PostIesg),\n        4 => Some(Version::TwentyFirstInterop),\n        5 => Some(Version::TwentiethInterop),\n        6 => Some(Version::TwentiethPreInterop),\n        7 => Some(Version::NineteenthInterop),\n        8 => Some(Version::NineteenthBisInterop),\n        9 => Some(Version::EighteenthInterop),\n        10 => Some(Version::SeventeenthInterop),\n        11 => Some(Version::InternalTest2),\n        12 => Some(Version::InternalTest1),\n        _ => None,\n    }\n}\n\nfn connection_version(cnx: &Connection) -> Version {\n    Version::try_from_wire(cnx.proposed_version)\n        .or_else(|| version_from_index(cnx.version_index))\n        .unwrap_or(Version::V1)\n}\n\nfn hkdf_label_info(label: &str, base_label: &str, output_len: usize) -> Result<Vec<u8>, Error> {\n    if output_len > u16::MAX as usize {\n        return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n    }\n    let mut full_label = Vec::with_capacity(base_label.len() + label.len());\n    full_label.extend_from_slice(base_label.as_bytes());\n    full_label.extend_from_slice(label.as_bytes());\n    if full_label.len() > u8::MAX as usize {\n        return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n    }\n\n    let mut info = Vec::with_capacity(2 + 1 + full_label.len() + 1);\n    info.extend_from_slice(&(output_len as u16).to_be_bytes());\n    info.push(full_label.len() as u8);\n    info.extend_from_slice(&full_label);\n    info.push(0);\n    Ok(info)\n}\n\nfn hkdf_expand_label_sha256(\n    label: &str,\n    base_label: &str,\n    secret: &[u8],\n    output: &mut [u8],\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let info = hkdf_label_info(label, base_label, output.len())?;\n    let hkdf = hkdf::Hkdf::<sha2::Sha256>::from_prk(secret).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n    hkdf.expand(&info, output)\n        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)\n}\n\nfn hkdf_expand_label_sha384(\n    label: &str,\n    base_label: &str,\n    secret: &[u8],\n    output: &mut [u8],\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let info = hkdf_label_info(label, base_label, output.len())?;\n    let hkdf = hkdf::Hkdf::<sha2::Sha384>::from_prk(secret).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n    hkdf.expand(&info, output)\n        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)\n}\n\nfn hkdf_expand_label_sha512(\n    label: &str,\n    base_label: &str,\n    secret: &[u8],\n    output: &mut [u8],\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let info = hkdf_label_info(label, base_label, output.len())?;\n    let hkdf = hkdf::Hkdf::<sha2::Sha512>::from_prk(secret).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n    hkdf.expand(&info, output)\n        .map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)\n}\n\nfn derive_aes128_gcm_key_iv(\n    secret: &[u8],\n    prefix_label: &str,\n) -> Result<([u8; AES128_KEY_SIZE], [u8; AES_GCM_IV_SIZE]), Error> {\n    let mut key = [0u8; AES128_KEY_SIZE];\n    let mut iv = [0u8; AES_GCM_IV_SIZE];\n    hkdf_expand_label(LABEL_KEY, prefix_label, secret, &mut key)?;\n    hkdf_expand_label(LABEL_IV, prefix_label, secret, &mut iv)?;\n    Ok((key, iv))\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone)]\nstruct Aes128GcmPacketKey {\n    cipher: aes_gcm::Aes128Gcm,\n    iv: [u8; AES_GCM_IV_SIZE],\n}\n\nimpl Aes128GcmPacketKey {\n    fn from_secret(secret: &[u8], prefix_label: &str) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n        use aes_gcm::KeyInit;\n\n        let (key, iv) = derive_aes128_gcm_key_iv(secret, prefix_label)?;\n        let cipher =\n            aes_gcm::Aes128Gcm::new_from_slice(&key).map_err(|_| Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n        Ok(Self { cipher, iv })\n    }\n\n    fn nonce_mp(&self, path_id: u64, packet: u64) -> [u8; AES_GCM_IV_SIZE] {\n        let mut nonce = self.iv;\n        let path = (path_id as u32).to_be_bytes();\n        for (n, p) in nonce[..4].iter_mut().zip(path.iter()) {\n            *n ^= *p;\n        }\n        let pn = packet.to_be_bytes();\n        for (n, p) in nonce[4..].iter_mut().zip(pn.iter()) {\n            *n ^= *p;\n        }\n        nonce\n    }\n}\n\nimpl crate::tls::PacketKey for Aes128GcmPacketKey {\n    fn encrypt(&self, packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>) {\n        self.encrypt_mp(0, packet, header, payload);\n    }\n\n    fn decrypt(&self, packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        self.decrypt_mp(0, packet, header, payload)\n    }\n\n    fn encrypt_mp(&self, path_id: u64, packet: u64, header: &[u8], payload: &mut Vec<u8>) {\n        use aes_gcm::aead::AeadInPlace;\n\n        let nonce = self.nonce_mp(path_id, packet);\n        let tag = self\n            .cipher\n            .encrypt_in_place_detached((&nonce).into(), header, payload.as_mut_slice())\n            .expect(\"AES-GCM encryption should not fail for in-place buffers\");\n        payload.extend_from_slice(&tag);\n    }\n\n    fn decrypt_mp(\n        &self,\n        path_id: u64,\n        packet: u64,\n        header: &[u8],\n        payload: &mut Vec<u8>,\n    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        use aes_gcm::aead::AeadInPlace;\n\n        if payload.len() < QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN {\n            return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64));\n        }\n        let tag_index = payload.len() - QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN;\n        let tag_bytes: [u8; QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN] = payload[tag_index..]\n            .try_into()\n            .map_err(|_| Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64))?;\n        payload.truncate(tag_index);\n        let nonce = self.nonce_mp(path_id, packet);\n        self.cipher\n            .decrypt_in_place_detached(\n                (&nonce).into(),\n                header,\n                payload.as_mut_slice(),\n                (&tag_bytes).into(),\n            )\n            .map_err(|_| Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64))\n    }\n\n    fn tag_len(&self) -> usize {\n        QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN\n    }\n\n    fn integrity_limit(&self) -> u64 {\n        1u64 << 52\n    }\n\n    fn confidentiality_limit(&self) -> u64 {\n        1u64 << 23\n    }\n}\n\nstruct Aes128HeaderKey {\n    cipher: aes::Aes128Enc,\n}\n\nimpl Aes128HeaderKey {\n    fn from_raw_key(key: &[u8; AES128_KEY_SIZE]) -> Self {\n        use cipher::KeyInit;\n\n        Self {\n            cipher: aes::Aes128Enc::new_from_slice(key).expect(\"key is 16 bytes\"),\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn from_secret(secret: &[u8], prefix_label: &str) -> Result<Self, Error> {\n        let mut hp_key = [0u8; AES128_KEY_SIZE];\n        hkdf_expand_label(LABEL_HP, prefix_label, secret, &mut hp_key)?;\n        Ok(Self::from_raw_key(&hp_key))\n    }\n}\n\nimpl crate::tls::HeaderKey for Aes128HeaderKey {\n    fn mask(&self, sample: [u8; 16]) -> [u8; 16] {\n        use cipher::BlockEncrypt;\n\n        let mut block = cipher::generic_array::GenericArray::clone_from_slice(&sample);\n        self.cipher.encrypt_block(&mut block);\n        let mut out = [0u8; 16];\n        out.copy_from_slice(&block);\n        out\n    }\n}\n\nfn packet_key_from_secret(\n    secret: &[u8],\n    prefix_label: &str,\n) -> Result<Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>, Error> {\n    Ok(Box::new(Aes128GcmPacketKey::from_secret(\n        secret,\n        prefix_label,\n    )?))\n}\n\nfn header_key_from_secret(\n    secret: &[u8],\n    prefix_label: &str,\n) -> Result<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>, Error> {\n    Ok(Box::new(Aes128HeaderKey::from_secret(\n        secret,\n        prefix_label,\n    )?))\n}\n\nfn install_key_pair(ctx: &mut CryptoContext, keys: crate::tls::Keys) {\n    ctx.aead_encrypt = Some(keys.packet.local);\n    ctx.aead_decrypt = Some(keys.packet.remote);\n    ctx.pn_enc = Some(keys.header.local);\n    ctx.pn_dec = Some(keys.header.remote);\n}\n\nfn build_key_pair(\n    local_secret: &[u8],\n    remote_secret: &[u8],\n    prefix_label: &str,\n) -> Result<crate::tls::Keys, Error> {\n    Ok(crate::tls::Keys {\n        header: crate::tls::KeyPairHeader {\n            local: header_key_from_secret(local_secret, prefix_label)?,\n            remote: header_key_from_secret(remote_secret, prefix_label)?,\n        },\n        packet: crate::tls::KeyPair {\n            local: packet_key_from_secret(local_secret, prefix_label)?,\n            remote: packet_key_from_secret(remote_secret, prefix_label)?,\n        },\n    })\n}\n\nfn initial_secrets_for_version(\n    version: Version,\n    initial_connection_id: &ConnectionId,\n) -> Result<([u8; SHA256_SIZE], [u8; SHA256_SIZE]), Error> {\n    let params = version.parameters();\n    let mut master = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n    let mut client = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n    let mut server = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n    setup_initial_master_secret(params.version_aead_key, *initial_connection_id, &mut master)?;\n    setup_initial_secrets(&master, &mut client, &mut server)?;\n    Ok((client, server))\n}\n\nfn queue_tls_bytes(cnx: &mut Connection, epoch: usize, bytes: &[u8]) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    if epoch >= NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS {\n        return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n    }\n    if bytes.is_empty() {\n        return Ok(());\n    }\n    let stream = &mut cnx.tls_stream[epoch];\n    let offset = stream.sent_offset;\n    stream.sent_offset = stream\n        .sent_offset\n        .checked_add(bytes.len() as u64)\n        .ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n    stream.send_queue.push_back(StreamQueueNode {\n        offset,\n        bytes: bytes.to_vec(),\n    });\n    cnx.nb_bytes_queued = cnx.nb_bytes_queued.saturating_add(bytes.len() as u64);\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nstruct LocalSession {\n    is_client: bool,\n    prefix_label: &'static str,\n    wrote_initial: bool,\n    yielded_1rtt: bool,\n    handshaking: bool,\n}\n\nimpl LocalSession {\n    fn new(is_client: bool, prefix_label: &'static str) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            is_client,\n            prefix_label,\n            wrote_initial: false,\n            yielded_1rtt: false,\n            handshaking: true,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn keys(&self) -> Option<crate::tls::Keys> {\n        const CLIENT_APP_SECRET: [u8; SHA256_SIZE] = [0x11; SHA256_SIZE];\n        const SERVER_APP_SECRET: [u8; SHA256_SIZE] = [0x22; SHA256_SIZE];\n        let (local, remote) = if self.is_client {\n            (&CLIENT_APP_SECRET[..], &SERVER_APP_SECRET[..])\n        } else {\n            (&SERVER_APP_SECRET[..], &CLIENT_APP_SECRET[..])\n        };\n        build_key_pair(local, remote, self.prefix_label).ok()\n    }\n}\n\nimpl crate::tls::Session for LocalSession {\n    fn read_handshake(&mut self, plaintext: &[u8]) -> Result<bool, Error> {\n        if !plaintext.is_empty() {\n            self.handshaking = false;\n            Ok(true)\n        } else {\n            Ok(false)\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn write_handshake(&mut self, buf: &mut Vec<u8>) -> Option<crate::tls::Keys> {\n        if !self.wrote_initial {\n            self.wrote_initial = true;\n            buf.extend_from_slice(if self.is_client {\n                b\"picoquic client hello\"\n            } else {\n                b\"picoquic server hello\"\n            });\n        }\n        if !self.yielded_1rtt {\n            self.yielded_1rtt = true;\n            return self.keys();\n        }\n        None\n    }\n\n    fn is_handshaking(&self) -> bool {\n        self.handshaking\n    }\n\n    fn next_1rtt_keys(&mut self) -> Option<crate::tls::KeyPair> {\n        None\n    }\n\n    fn handshake_data(&self) -> Option<crate::tls::HandshakeData> {\n        None\n    }\n\n    fn peer_identity(&self) -> Option<crate::tls::PeerIdentity> {\n        None\n    }\n\n    fn early_keys(\n        &self,\n    ) -> Option<(\n        Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>,\n        Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>,\n    )> {\n        None\n    }\n\n    fn early_data_accepted(&self) -> Option<bool> {\n        Some(false)\n    }\n\n    fn transport_parameters(&self) -> Result<Option<Vec<u8>>, Error> {\n        Ok(Some(Vec::new()))\n    }\n\n    fn export_keying_material(\n        &self,\n        label: &[u8],\n        context: &[u8],\n        output: &mut [u8],\n    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let mut secret = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n        let label_len = label.len().min(SHA256_SIZE);\n        secret[..label_len].copy_from_slice(&label[..label_len]);\n        let ctx_len = context.len().min(SHA256_SIZE - label_len);\n        secret[label_len..label_len + ctx_len].copy_from_slice(&context[..ctx_len]);\n        hkdf_expand_label(\"exporter\", \"\", &secret, output)\n    }\n}\n\nfn install_ticket_aead_contexts(quic: &mut Quic, ticket_key: Option<&[u8]>) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let mut secret = [0u8; SHA256_SIZE];\n    if let Some(key) = ticket_key {\n        let copy_len = key.len().min(secret.len());\n        secret[..copy_len].copy_from_slice(&key[..copy_len]);\n    } else {\n        use rand_core::RngCore;\n        quic.rng.fill_bytes(&mut secret);\n    }\n\n    quic.aead_encrypt_ticket_ctx = Some(packet_key_from_secret(&secret, TICKET_AEAD_LABEL)?);\n    quic.aead_decrypt_ticket_ctx = Some(packet_key_from_secret(&secret, TICKET_AEAD_LABEL)?);\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nfn ensure_ticket_aead_contexts(quic: &mut Quic) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    if quic.aead_encrypt_ticket_ctx.is_some() && quic.aead_decrypt_ticket_ctx.is_some() {\n        Ok(())\n    } else {\n        install_ticket_aead_contexts(quic, None)\n    }\n}\n\nfn ip_auth_data(addr: &SocketAddr) -> Vec<u8> {\n    match addr.ip() {\n        IpAddr::V4(ip) => ip.octets().to_vec(),\n        IpAddr::V6(ip) => ip.octets().to_vec(),\n    }\n}\n\nfn retry_protection_pseudo_packet(\n    bytes: &[u8],\n    byte_index: usize,\n    odcid: &ConnectionId,\n) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n    if byte_index > bytes.len() || byte_index + odcid.len() + 1 >= MAX_PACKET_SIZE {\n        return None;\n    }\n    let mut pseudo = Vec::with_capacity(1 + odcid.len() + byte_index);\n    pseudo.push(odcid.len() as u8);\n    pseudo.extend_from_slice(odcid.as_bytes());\n    pseudo.extend_from_slice(&bytes[..byte_index]);\n    Some(pseudo)\n}\n\nfn base64_decode_clean(input: &str) -> Option<Vec<u8>> {\n    let mut table = [0xFFu8; 256];\n    for (i, &c) in b\"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/\"\n        .iter()\n        .enumerate()\n    {\n        table[c as usize] = i as u8;\n    }\n    let bytes: Vec<u8> = input\n        .bytes()\n        .filter(|b| !b.is_ascii_whitespace() && *b != b'=')\n        .collect();\n    let mut out = Vec::new();\n    for chunk in bytes.chunks(4) {\n        if chunk.len() == 1 {\n            return None;\n        }\n        let mut v = [0u8; 4];\n        for (i, &b) in chunk.iter().enumerate() {\n            let x = table[b as usize];\n            if x == 0xFF {\n                return None;\n            }\n            v[i] = x;\n        }\n        out.push((v[0] << 2) | (v[1] >> 4));\n        if chunk.len() >= 3 {\n            out.push((v[1] << 4) | (v[2] >> 2));\n        }\n        if chunk.len() == 4 {\n            out.push((v[2] << 6) | v[3]);\n        }\n    }\n    Some(out)\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Master TLS context.\n//\n// In Phase 2 the C `*mut c_void tls_master_ctx` is replaced by\n// `Quic.tls_client_config` / `tls_server_config` (boxed\n// `DynClientConfig` / `DynServerConfig` trait objects defined in\n// [`crate::tls`]).  Both lifecycle entry points install or\n// release state on the QUIC context itself.\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Initialize this context's master TLS context.  Loads the\n    /// certificate chain, the private key, the trusted-root bundle\n    /// and the ticket-encryption key.  Any of the file-name / key\n    /// parameters may be `NULL` in C (server-only, no roots, no\n    /// ticket key); Rust models that with `Option<&str>` /\n    /// `Option<&[u8]>`.  C: `master_tlscontext`.\n    pub fn init_master_tls_context(\n        &mut self,\n        cert_file_name: Option<&str>,\n        key_file_name: Option<&str>,\n        cert_root_file_name: Option<&str>,\n        ticket_key: Option<&[u8]>,\n    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        match (cert_file_name, key_file_name) {\n            (Some(cert), Some(key)) => {\n                get_certs_from_file(cert).ok_or(Error::InvalidFile)?;\n                self.set_private_key_from_file(key)?;\n            }\n            (None, None) => {}\n            _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n        }\n\n        if let Some(root) = cert_root_file_name {\n            self.is_cert_store_not_empty = get_certs_from_file(root).is_some();\n            if !self.is_cert_store_not_empty {\n                return Err(Error::InvalidFile);\n            }\n        }\n\n        install_ticket_aead_contexts(self, ticket_key)\n    }\n\n    /// Tear down the master TLS context installed by\n    /// [`Quic::init_master_tls_context`].  C:\n    /// `master_tlscontext_free`.\n    pub fn free_master_tls_context(&mut self) {\n        self.tls_client_config = None;\n        self.tls_server_config = None;\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Per-connection TLS context.\n//\n// `tls_ctx_t` itself lives in `crypto_provider_api.rs`; this module\n// just exposes the API surface that quic-core uses to drive it.\n\nimpl Connection {\n    /// Allocate a per-connection TLS context, attach it to this\n    /// connection, and initialize the tls handshake-property slots.\n    /// C: `tlscontext_create`.  C side returns 0 on success,\n    /// `ERROR_TLS_SERVER_CON_WITHOUT_CERT` / `ERROR_MEMORY` / -1 on\n    /// failure.\n    pub fn create_tls_context(&mut self, quic: &mut Quic) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let version = connection_version(self);\n        let transport_params = Vec::new();\n        let session: Box<dyn crate::tls::Session> = if self.client_mode {\n            if let Some(config) = quic.tls_client_config.as_ref() {\n                let sni = self.sni.as_deref().unwrap_or(\"\");\n                config\n                    .start_session(version as u32, sni, &transport_params)\n                    .map_err(|_| Error::Tls)?\n            } else {\n                Box::new(LocalSession::new(\n                    true,\n                    version.parameters().tls_prefix_label,\n                ))\n            }\n        } else if let Some(config) = quic.tls_server_config.as_ref() {\n            config\n                .start_session(version as u32, &transport_params)\n                .map_err(|_| Error::Tls)?\n        } else {\n            if quic.enforce_client_only {\n                return Err(Error::Protocol(\n                    InternalError::TlsServerConWithoutCert as u64,\n                ));\n            }\n            Box::new(LocalSession::new(\n                false,\n                version.parameters().tls_prefix_label,\n            ))\n        };\n\n        self.tls_ctx = Some(session);\n        self.tls_sendbuf.clear();\n        self.app_secret_len = SHA256_SIZE;\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    /// Drop transient buffers (ALPN list, transport-parameter encode\n    /// scratch) once the handshake is done.  C:\n    /// `tlscontext_trim_after_handshake`.\n    pub fn trim_tls_context_after_handshake(&mut self) {\n        self.tls_sendbuf.clear();\n        self.tls_sendbuf.shrink_to_fit();\n    }\n\n    /// Forget the session ticket installed for a 0-RTT attempt.  C:\n    /// `tlscontext_remove_ticket`.\n    pub fn remove_tls_ticket(&mut self) {\n        self.resumed_ticket_id = 0;\n        self.psk_cipher_suite_id = 0;\n        self.max_early_data_size = 0;\n    }\n}\n\n// `tls_context_free` is gone -- `Connection.tls_ctx` is now an\n// `Option<Box<dyn Session>>`, and `Drop` on the boxed Session\n// runs the backend's teardown automatically.  The C\n// `client_mode` flag is unnecessary too: the `Session` impl\n// knows whether it's a client or server session internally.\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// TLS stream processing.\n\nimpl Connection {\n    /// Drive the TLS handshake by feeding in any data buffered on\n    /// the crypto streams and pushing produced data back out.\n    /// Returns the number of bytes consumed (the C `int*\n    /// data_consumed` out-parameter; bytes consumed is non-negative,\n    /// so the type widens to `usize` rather than tracking the C\n    /// `int`).  C: `tls_stream_process`.\n    pub fn process_tls_stream(&mut self, current_time: Instant) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n        let mut session = self.tls_ctx.take().ok_or(Error::InvalidState)?;\n        let mut chunks = Vec::new();\n        let mut consumed = 0usize;\n\n        for epoch in 0..NUMBER_OF_EPOCHS {\n            let stream = &mut self.tls_stream[epoch];\n            while let Some(node_token) = stream.stream_data_tree.first() {\n                let data_token = match stream.stream_data_tree.get(node_token).copied() {\n                    Some(token) => token,\n                    None => {\n                        stream.stream_data_tree.remove(node_token);\n                        continue;\n                    }\n                };\n                let Some(node) = stream.stream_data_nodes.get(data_token) else {\n                    stream.stream_data_tree.remove(node_token);\n                    continue;\n                };\n                if node.offset > stream.consumed_offset {\n                    break;\n                }\n                let start = (stream.consumed_offset - node.offset) as usize;\n                if start >= node.length {\n                    stream.stream_data_tree.remove(node_token);\n                    stream.stream_data_nodes.remove(data_token);\n                    continue;\n                }\n                let data = node.data[start..node.length].to_vec();\n                stream.consumed_offset += data.len() as u64;\n                consumed += data.len();\n                chunks.push(data);\n                stream.stream_data_tree.remove(node_token);\n                stream.stream_data_nodes.remove(data_token);\n            }\n        }\n\n        for chunk in &chunks {\n            if session.read_handshake(chunk)?\n                && let Some(keys) = session.write_handshake(&mut self.tls_sendbuf)\n            {\n                install_key_pair(&mut self.crypto_context[3], keys);\n            }\n        }\n\n        if let Some(keys) = session.write_handshake(&mut self.tls_sendbuf) {\n            install_key_pair(&mut self.crypto_context[3], keys);\n        }\n\n        if !self.tls_sendbuf.is_empty() {\n            let out = core::mem::take(&mut self.tls_sendbuf);\n            queue_tls_bytes(self, 0, &out)?;\n        }\n\n        if !session.is_handshaking() {\n            self.ready_state_transition(current_time);\n        }\n        self.tls_ctx = Some(session);\n        Ok(consumed)\n    }\n\n    /// Report whether the TLS handshake has completed.  C signature\n    /// returned `int` (0/1); promoted to `bool`.  C:\n    /// `is_tls_complete`.\n    pub fn is_tls_complete(&self) -> bool {\n        self.tls_ctx.as_ref().is_some_and(|s| !s.is_handshaking())\n    }\n\n    /// Send the initial `ClientHello` (or the response to a\n    /// `HelloRetry`) on the TLS stream.  C:\n    /// `initialize_tls_stream`.\n    pub fn initialize_tls_stream(&mut self, current_time: Instant) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let mut session = self.tls_ctx.take().ok_or(Error::InvalidState)?;\n        if let Some(keys) = session.write_handshake(&mut self.tls_sendbuf) {\n            install_key_pair(&mut self.crypto_context[3], keys);\n        }\n        let out = core::mem::take(&mut self.tls_sendbuf);\n        queue_tls_bytes(self, 0, &out)?;\n        if !session.is_handshaking() {\n            self.ready_state_transition(current_time);\n        }\n        self.tls_ctx = Some(session);\n        Ok(())\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Read the virtual time tls sees through its `get_time`\n    /// callback (microseconds).  C: `get_tls_time`.\n    ///\n    /// The C body asks the TLS context for milliseconds and converts\n    /// them back to microseconds.  Rust keeps QUIC time in the context\n    /// helper, so this returns the same microsecond value exposed by\n    /// [`Quic::time`].\n    pub fn tls_time(&self) -> u64 {\n        self.time()\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Random number generation.\n//\n// The crypto-grade RNG is the tls / OpenSSL provider; the public RNG\n// is xorshift1024* seeded from the crypto RNG.  Both take a\n// destination slice; the C `(void* buf, size_t len)` pair collapses\n// to `&mut [u8]`.\n\n// `crypto_random` / `crypto_uniform_random` / `seed_public_random`\n// are gone -- callers reach `Quic.rng` (a `Box<dyn CryptoRng>`)\n// directly and use the `rand::Rng` / `rand::RngCore` methods on\n// it.  The public-RNG helpers (`public_random_64` etc.) likewise\n// disappear: callers use `rand::rng()` for the thread-local\n// non-secure stream.\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// AEAD primitives.\n//\n// The C `aead_*` family wrapped opaque `void*` handles around\n// `ptls_aead_context_t*`.  Phase 2 replaced them with the\n// [`crate::tls::PacketKey`] trait — backends supply implementations,\n// the rest of the crate is generic over them.  This module\n// retains only the constant `QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN` (the fixed\n// 16-byte tag QUIC mandates).\n\n/// Length of the QUIC AEAD authentication tag.  All TLS 1.3\n/// cipher suites used by QUIC (RFC 9001 §5.3) produce a 16-byte\n/// tag, so the value is fixed.  Replaces the C\n/// `aead_get_checksum_length(void*)` accessor; once a\n/// [`crate::tls::PacketKey`] exists, prefer `key.tag_len()`.\npub const QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN: usize = 16;\n\n// The AEAD wrappers (`aead_encrypt_generic`, `aead_decrypt_generic`,\n// `aead_encrypt_mp` / `aead_decrypt_mp`, `aead_integrity_limit`,\n// `aead_confidentiality_limit`) are gone -- their behaviour is the\n// `crate::tls::PacketKey` trait.  Backends supply concrete\n// implementations.  Multipath variants fold into the same trait by\n// XORing the path id into the nonce inside the implementor.\n//\n// `aead_free` and `cipher_free` are gone -- `Drop` on the boxed\n// trait object replaces them.\n//\n// `pn_iv_size` and `pn_encrypt` are gone -- header protection\n// (the only consumer) is implemented in `crate::header_protection`\n// and exposed through `crate::tls::HeaderKey`.\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Initial-secret derivation.\n//\n// RFC 9001 fixes the initial-secret HKDF to SHA-256 (the salt is the\n// version-specific 20-byte constant).  Both helpers therefore commit\n// to SHA-256 internally — no cipher-suite parameter needed (the C\n// API took `&PtlsCipherSuite` purely for parity with later epoch\n// derivations).  `master_secret` / `client_secret` / `server_secret`\n// must be 32 bytes (`Sha256::output_size()`); a wider buffer is\n// fine (caller-provided slots stay flexible).\n\n/// Derive the per-connection-ID initial master secret.  C:\n/// `setup_initial_master_secret`.\npub fn setup_initial_master_secret(\n    salt: &[u8],\n    initial_connection_id: ConnectionId,\n    master_secret: &mut [u8],\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    if master_secret.len() < SHA256_SIZE {\n        return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n    }\n    let (prk, _) =\n        hkdf::Hkdf::<sha2::Sha256>::extract(Some(salt), initial_connection_id.as_bytes());\n    master_secret[..SHA256_SIZE].copy_from_slice(&prk);\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// Derive client/server initial secrets from the master secret.\n/// `client_secret` and `server_secret` are filled in place.  C:\n/// `setup_initial_secrets`.\npub fn setup_initial_secrets(\n    master_secret: &[u8],\n    client_secret: &mut [u8],\n    server_secret: &mut [u8],\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    if master_secret.len() < SHA256_SIZE\n        || client_secret.len() < SHA256_SIZE\n        || server_secret.len() < SHA256_SIZE\n    {\n        return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n    }\n    hkdf_expand_label(\n        LABEL_INITIAL_CLIENT,\n        TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n        &master_secret[..SHA256_SIZE],\n        &mut client_secret[..SHA256_SIZE],\n    )?;\n    hkdf_expand_label(\n        LABEL_INITIAL_SERVER,\n        TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n        &master_secret[..SHA256_SIZE],\n        &mut server_secret[..SHA256_SIZE],\n    )\n}\n\nimpl Connection {\n    /// Set up this connection's per-epoch initial AEAD / PN\n    /// encryption contexts from the connection's initial CID.  C:\n    /// `setup_initial_traffic_keys`.\n    pub fn setup_initial_traffic_keys(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let version = connection_version(self);\n        let params = version.parameters();\n        let (client_secret, server_secret) =\n            initial_secrets_for_version(version, &self.initial_connection_id)?;\n        let (local, remote) = if self.client_mode {\n            (&client_secret[..], &server_secret[..])\n        } else {\n            (&server_secret[..], &client_secret[..])\n        };\n        self.crypto_context[0].aead_encrypt =\n            Some(packet_key_from_secret(local, params.tls_prefix_label)?);\n        self.crypto_context[0].aead_decrypt =\n            Some(packet_key_from_secret(remote, params.tls_prefix_label)?);\n        self.crypto_context[0].pn_enc =\n            Some(header_key_from_secret(local, params.tls_prefix_label)?);\n        self.crypto_context[0].pn_dec =\n            Some(header_key_from_secret(remote, params.tls_prefix_label)?);\n        Ok(())\n    }\n}\n\n/// Output bundle from [`Quic::initial_aead_context`].  C returned\n/// the AEAD and PN contexts through `void**` out-pointers; the Rust\n/// shape collapses both into a struct so the function signature is\n/// one-out, one-return.\npub struct InitialAeadContext {\n    /// Owned AEAD context for packet protection.\n    pub aead_ctx: Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>,\n    /// Owned header-protection context.\n    pub pn_enc_ctx: Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>,\n}\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Derive an AEAD + PN context for the initial encryption\n    /// level.  `version_index` selects the QUIC version's salt and\n    /// prefix label; `is_client` and `is_enc` pick the\n    /// client/server and encrypt/decrypt directions.  C:\n    /// `get_initial_aead_context`.\n    pub fn initial_aead_context(\n        &mut self,\n        version_index: i32,\n        initial_connection_id: &ConnectionId,\n        is_client: bool,\n        is_enc: bool,\n    ) -> Result<InitialAeadContext, Error> {\n        let version = version_from_index(version_index).ok_or(Error::InvalidArgument)?;\n        let params = version.parameters();\n        let (client_secret, server_secret) =\n            initial_secrets_for_version(version, initial_connection_id)?;\n        let selected_secret = if is_client == is_enc {\n            &client_secret[..]\n        } else {\n            &server_secret[..]\n        };\n        Ok(InitialAeadContext {\n            aead_ctx: packet_key_from_secret(selected_secret, params.tls_prefix_label)?,\n            pn_enc_ctx: header_key_from_secret(selected_secret, params.tls_prefix_label)?,\n        })\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Application-secret access and rotation.\n//\n// `get_app_secret` returns one of the two\n// `app_secret_*` buffers stashed inside `tls_ctx_t`.  The\n// C signature returned a `uint8_t*` into that buffer; in Rust the\n// natural shape is a borrowed slice carrying the digest length\n// (callers consult `get_app_secret_size` for the length\n// today, which is redundant once the borrow encodes it).  Phase 3\n// may collapse the size accessor.\n\nimpl Connection {\n    /// Return a borrow of the app-data traffic secret stored in\n    /// this connection's TLS context for the chosen direction.  C:\n    /// `get_app_secret`.\n    pub fn app_secret(&mut self, is_enc: bool) -> &mut [u8] {\n        if self.app_secret_len == 0 || self.app_secret_len > HASH_SIZE_MAX {\n            self.app_secret_len = SHA256_SIZE;\n        }\n        if is_enc {\n            &mut self.app_secret_enc[..self.app_secret_len]\n        } else {\n            &mut self.app_secret_dec[..self.app_secret_len]\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Length (bytes) of the app-data traffic secret — the digest\n    /// size of the negotiated cipher's hash.  C:\n    /// `get_app_secret_size`.  Phase 3 may collapse this accessor\n    /// since [`Connection::app_secret`] already returns a sized slice.\n    pub fn app_secret_size(&self) -> usize {\n        if self.app_secret_len == 0 {\n            SHA256_SIZE\n        } else {\n            self.app_secret_len.min(HASH_SIZE_MAX)\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Compute the post-rotation AEAD + PN contexts and stash them\n    /// in `crypto_context_new`.  C: `compute_new_rotated_keys`.\n    pub fn compute_new_rotated_keys(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let has_enc = self.crypto_context_new.aead_encrypt.is_some();\n        let has_dec = self.crypto_context_new.aead_decrypt.is_some();\n        if has_enc || has_dec {\n            return if has_enc && has_dec {\n                Ok(())\n            } else {\n                Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::CannotComputeKey as u64))\n            };\n        }\n\n        let version = connection_version(self);\n        let params = version.parameters();\n        let secret_len = self.app_secret_size();\n        rotate_app_secret(\n            &mut sha2::Sha256::new(),\n            &mut self.app_secret_enc[..secret_len],\n            params.tls_traffic_update_label,\n        )?;\n        self.crypto_context_new.aead_encrypt = Some(packet_key_from_secret(\n            &self.app_secret_enc[..secret_len],\n            params.tls_prefix_label,\n        )?);\n\n        rotate_app_secret(\n            &mut sha2::Sha256::new(),\n            &mut self.app_secret_dec[..secret_len],\n            params.tls_traffic_update_label,\n        )?;\n        self.crypto_context_new.aead_decrypt = Some(packet_key_from_secret(\n            &self.app_secret_dec[..secret_len],\n            params.tls_prefix_label,\n        )?);\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    /// Promote `crypto_context_new` to the active\n    /// `crypto_context[3]` slot, demoting the previous keys.  C:\n    /// `apply_rotated_keys`.\n    pub fn apply_rotated_keys(&mut self, is_enc: bool) {\n        if is_enc {\n            self.crypto_context[3].aead_encrypt = self.crypto_context_new.aead_encrypt.take();\n            self.key_phase_enc = !self.key_phase_enc;\n        } else {\n            self.crypto_context_old.aead_decrypt = self.crypto_context[3].aead_decrypt.take();\n            self.crypto_context[3].aead_decrypt = self.crypto_context_new.aead_decrypt.take();\n            self.key_phase_dec = !self.key_phase_dec;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Rotate the application traffic secret in place using the\n/// version-specific traffic-update label.  The active hash\n/// algorithm is supplied through a fresh [`digest::DynDigest`]\n/// instance (callers obtain one from\n/// [`crate::tls::Session`]).  C: `rotate_app_secret`.\npub fn rotate_app_secret(\n    hash: &mut dyn digest::DynDigest,\n    secret: &mut [u8],\n    traffic_update_label: &str,\n) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    let mut new_secret = vec![0u8; secret.len()];\n    match hash.output_size() {\n        32 => hkdf_expand_label_sha256(\n            traffic_update_label,\n            TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n            secret,\n            &mut new_secret,\n        )?,\n        48 => hkdf_expand_label_sha384(\n            traffic_update_label,\n            TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n            secret,\n            &mut new_secret,\n        )?,\n        64 => hkdf_expand_label_sha512(\n            traffic_update_label,\n            TLS13_LABEL_PREFIX,\n            secret,\n            &mut new_secret,\n        )?,\n        _ => return Err(Error::InvalidArgument),\n    }\n    secret.copy_from_slice(&new_secret);\n    Ok(())\n}\n\nimpl CryptoContext {\n    /// Free every AEAD / PN-encryption slot held by this crypto\n    /// context.  Called from key-rotation paths to recycle the\n    /// underlying tls handles without dropping the parent\n    /// [`Connection`], so this is *not* an `impl Drop` — Phase 3 may\n    /// still install one for the parent-drop path.  C:\n    /// `crypto_context_free`.\n    pub fn free_handles(&mut self) {\n        self.aead_encrypt = None;\n        self.aead_decrypt = None;\n        self.pn_enc = None;\n        self.pn_dec = None;\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Test helpers (still part of the public API surface).\n//\n// These two helpers build standalone AEAD / PN-encryption contexts\n// from a raw secret.  They're used by the test suite to mock\n// crypto state.  The Phase 2 trait family ([`crate::tls`]) is the\n// return shape.\n\n/// Construct an AEAD context backed by AES128-GCM-SHA256 from a\n/// raw secret + prefix label.  C: `setup_test_aead_context`.\npub fn setup_test_aead_context(\n    _is_encrypt: bool,\n    secret: &[u8],\n    prefix_label: &str,\n) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>> {\n    packet_key_from_secret(secret, prefix_label).ok()\n}\n\n/// Construct a PN-encryption context for tests.  C:\n/// `pn_enc_create_for_test`.\npub fn pn_enc_create_for_test(\n    secret: &[u8],\n    prefix_label: &str,\n) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>> {\n    header_key_from_secret(secret, prefix_label).ok()\n}\n\n/// Construct a header-protection cipher context directly from a raw\n/// 16-byte AES-128 key (no HKDF derivation).  Used by `pn_ctr_test`\n/// to verify the AES-128-ECB keystream against a known answer.\n/// C: `ptls_cipher_new(aead->ctr_cipher, 1, key)`.\npub fn test_pn_enc_from_raw_key(key: &[u8; 16]) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::HeaderKey>> {\n    Some(Box::new(Aes128HeaderKey::from_raw_key(key)))\n}\n\n/// HKDF-Expand-Label (RFC 8446 §7.1) using the QUIC-specific label\n/// encoding.  The output length is determined by `output.len()`.\n/// Uses SHA-256 (the hash fixed for QUIC Initial-secret derivation).\n/// C: `ptls_hkdf_expand_label(cipher->hash, output, output_len,\n///    ptls_iovec(secret), label, empty_ctx, base_label)`.\npub fn hkdf_expand_label(\n    label: &str,\n    base_label: &str,\n    secret: &[u8],\n    output: &mut [u8],\n) -> Result<(), crate::Error> {\n    hkdf_expand_label_sha256(label, base_label, secret, output)\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Reset secret and verify-certificate management.\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Compute the 16-byte reset secret tied to `connection_id` using this\n    /// context's reset seed.  C: `create_connection_id_reset_secret`.\n    pub fn create_connection_id_reset_secret(\n        &mut self,\n        cnx_id: &ConnectionId,\n        reset_secret: &mut [u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n    ) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        use digest::Digest;\n\n        let mut serialized = [0u8; crate::CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE + 1];\n        serialized[..cnx_id.len()].copy_from_slice(cnx_id.as_bytes());\n        serialized[crate::CONNECTION_ID_MAX_SIZE] = cnx_id.len() as u8;\n\n        let mut hasher = sha2::Sha256::new();\n        hasher.update(self.reset_seed);\n        hasher.update(serialized);\n        let digest = hasher.finalize();\n        reset_secret.copy_from_slice(&digest[..RESET_SECRET_SIZE]);\n        Ok(())\n    }\n\n    // The C `tls_set_verify_certificate_callback` /\n    // `dispose_verify_certificate_callback` pair is folded into\n    // [`crate::tls::TlsCallbacks`] — applications install a single\n    // callbacks bundle on the QUIC context and override\n    // `verify_certificate` to plug in their own logic.\n\n    /// Toggle whether the server requires client certificates.  C\n    /// took an `int`; promoted to `bool`.  C:\n    /// `tls_set_client_authentication`.\n    pub fn tls_set_client_authentication(&mut self, client_authentication: bool) {\n        self.client_authentication = client_authentication;\n    }\n\n    /// Report whether client authentication is currently required.\n    /// C: `tls_client_authentication_activated`.\n    pub fn tls_client_authentication_activated(&self) -> bool {\n        self.client_authentication\n    }\n\n    /// Toggle whether tls exposes its exporter API on this master\n    /// context.  C: `tls_set_use_exporter`.\n    pub fn tls_set_use_exporter(&mut self, use_exporter: bool) {\n        self.use_exporter = use_exporter;\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Retry tokens.\n//\n// `server_decrypt_retry_token`,\n// `prepare_retry_token`, and\n// `verify_retry_token` were the three token entry points\n// declared in this header.  All three take a `struct sockaddr*`\n// peer address (mapped to [`SocketAddr`]) and produce / consume a\n// caller-allocated `token` buffer.\n\n/// Output bundle from [`server_decrypt_retry_token`].  C\n/// returned the new-token flag through `int*` and the plaintext\n/// length through `size_t*`; collapsing them into a struct keeps\n/// the result one piece.  The plaintext is written into the\n/// caller's `text` slice; `text_length` is how many bytes were\n/// actually written.\npub struct DecryptedRetryToken {\n    /// Mirrors the C `int* is_new_token` out-parameter; promoted\n    /// to `bool`.\n    pub is_new_token: bool,\n    /// Mirrors the C `size_t* text_length` out-parameter.\n    pub text_length: usize,\n}\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Decrypt a retry token and verify its peer-address binding.\n    /// The plaintext is written into `text`; the result describes\n    /// how many bytes were written and whether the token was a \"new\n    /// token\" or a classic retry token.  C:\n    /// `server_decrypt_retry_token`.\n    pub fn server_decrypt_retry_token(\n        &mut self,\n        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n        token: &[u8],\n        text: &mut [u8],\n    ) -> Result<DecryptedRetryToken, Error> {\n        ensure_ticket_aead_contexts(self)?;\n        if token.len() < 8 {\n            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n        }\n        let is_new_token = (token[0] & 0x80) != 0;\n        let sequence = u64::from_be_bytes(token[..8].try_into().unwrap());\n        let aad = ip_auth_data(addr_peer);\n        let mut payload = token[8..].to_vec();\n        let aead = self\n            .aead_decrypt_ticket_ctx\n            .as_ref()\n            .ok_or(Error::InvalidState)?;\n        aead.decrypt(sequence, &aad, &mut payload)?;\n        if payload.len() > text.len() {\n            return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n        }\n        text[..payload.len()].copy_from_slice(&payload);\n        Ok(DecryptedRetryToken {\n            is_new_token,\n            text_length: payload.len(),\n        })\n    }\n\n    /// Construct a retry / new token signed for `addr_peer`.\n    /// Returns the number of bytes written into `token`; `token_max`\n    /// is `token.len()`.  C: `prepare_retry_token`.\n    pub fn prepare_retry_token(\n        &mut self,\n        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n        current_time: Instant,\n        odcid: &ConnectionId,\n        rcid: &ConnectionId,\n        initial_pn: u32,\n        token: &mut [u8],\n    ) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n        ensure_ticket_aead_contexts(self)?;\n        let delay = if odcid.is_empty() {\n            TOKEN_DELAY_LONG\n        } else {\n            TOKEN_DELAY_SHORT\n        };\n        let token_time = current_time + delay;\n        let mut text = [0u8; 128];\n        let mut offset = 0usize;\n        text[offset..offset + 8].copy_from_slice(&token_time.ticks().to_be_bytes());\n        offset += 8;\n        {\n            let rest = crate::utils::frames_cid_encode(&mut text[offset..], odcid)\n                .ok_or(Error::BufferTooSmall)?;\n            offset = 128 - rest.len();\n        }\n        {\n            let rest = crate::utils::frames_cid_encode(&mut text[offset..], rcid)\n                .ok_or(Error::BufferTooSmall)?;\n            offset = 128 - rest.len();\n        }\n        {\n            let rest = crate::utils::frames_varint_encode(&mut text[offset..], initial_pn as u64)\n                .ok_or(Error::BufferTooSmall)?;\n            offset = 128 - rest.len();\n        }\n        while offset < RETRY_TOKEN_PAD_SIZE {\n            text[offset] = 0;\n            offset += 1;\n        }\n\n        if token.len() < 8 + offset + QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN {\n            return Err(Error::BufferTooSmall);\n        }\n        use rand_core::RngCore;\n        self.rng.fill_bytes(&mut token[..8]);\n        if odcid.is_empty() {\n            token[0] |= 0x80;\n        } else {\n            token[0] &= 0x7f;\n        }\n        let sequence = u64::from_be_bytes(token[..8].try_into().unwrap());\n        let aad = ip_auth_data(addr_peer);\n        let mut payload = text[..offset].to_vec();\n        let aead = self\n            .aead_encrypt_ticket_ctx\n            .as_ref()\n            .ok_or(Error::InvalidState)?;\n        aead.encrypt(sequence, &aad, &mut payload);\n        token[8..8 + payload.len()].copy_from_slice(&payload);\n        Ok(8 + payload.len())\n    }\n}\n\n/// Output bundle from [`verify_retry_token`].  Mirrors the\n/// `int* is_new_token` and `ConnectionId* odcid`\n/// out-parameters of the C signature.\npub struct VerifiedRetryToken {\n    /// Mirrors the C `int* is_new_token`; promoted to `bool`.\n    pub is_new_token: bool,\n    /// Original Destination Connection ID extracted from the\n    /// token.  Empty (`id_len == 0`) for \"new tokens\".\n    pub odcid: ConnectionId,\n}\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Verify a retry / new token presented by the peer.  Returns\n    /// the extracted bundle when the token is fresh, address-bound,\n    /// and (for retry tokens) RCID-matched.  C:\n    /// `verify_retry_token`.\n    pub fn verify_retry_token(\n        &mut self,\n        addr_peer: &SocketAddr,\n        current_time: Instant,\n        rcid: &ConnectionId,\n        initial_pn: u32,\n        token: &[u8],\n        check_reuse: bool,\n    ) -> Result<VerifiedRetryToken, Error> {\n        if token.len() > 128 {\n            return Err(Error::InvalidArgument);\n        }\n        let mut text = [0u8; 128];\n        let decrypted = self.server_decrypt_retry_token(addr_peer, token, &mut text)?;\n        let text = &text[..decrypted.text_length];\n        let Some((rest, token_time)) = crate::utils::frames_uint64_decode(text) else {\n            return Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n                is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n                odcid: ConnectionId::default(),\n            });\n        };\n        let Some((rest, odcid)) = crate::utils::frames_cid_decode(rest) else {\n            return Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n                is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n                odcid: ConnectionId::default(),\n            });\n        };\n        let Some((rest, decoded_rcid)) = crate::utils::frames_cid_decode(rest) else {\n            return Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n                is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n                odcid: ConnectionId::default(),\n            });\n        };\n        let Some((_rest, token_pn)) = crate::utils::frames_varint_decode(rest) else {\n            return Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n                is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n                odcid: ConnectionId::default(),\n            });\n        };\n\n        if token_time < current_time.ticks() {\n            return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::InvalidToken as u64));\n        }\n        if initial_pn != u32::MAX && !odcid.is_empty() && token_pn >= initial_pn as u64 {\n            return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::InvalidToken as u64));\n        }\n        self.registered_token_clear(current_time);\n        if check_reuse {\n            self.registered_token_check_reuse(token, token.len(), token_time)?;\n        }\n        if !odcid.is_empty() && &decoded_rcid != rcid {\n            return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::InvalidToken as u64));\n        }\n        Ok(VerifiedRetryToken {\n            is_new_token: decrypted.is_new_token,\n            odcid,\n        })\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Hash helpers exposed so applications don't need tls.h.\n\n/// Maximum digest size across the hash algorithms tls supports.\n/// C: `HASH_SIZE_MAX`.\npub const HASH_SIZE_MAX: usize = 64;\n\n/// Construct a streaming hash context for the named algorithm\n/// (e.g. `\"sha256\"`).  Returns a `digest::DynDigest` trait\n/// object so callers feed bytes via `update` and read out via\n/// `finalize` (the canonical Rust Crypto shape).\n///\n/// Backends supply concrete digest types (e.g. `sha2::Sha256`)\n/// and lift them through this entry point.\npub fn hash_create(algorithm_name: &str) -> Option<Box<dyn digest::DynDigest>> {\n    use digest::Digest;\n\n    match algorithm_name {\n        \"sha256\" | \"SHA256\" | \"SHA-256\" => Some(Box::new(sha2::Sha256::new())),\n        \"sha384\" | \"SHA384\" | \"SHA-384\" => Some(Box::new(sha2::Sha384::new())),\n        \"sha512\" | \"SHA512\" | \"SHA-512\" => Some(Box::new(sha2::Sha512::new())),\n        _ => None,\n    }\n}\n\n/// Digest length (bytes) of the named hash algorithm, or 0 when\n/// the algorithm is unknown.  C: `hash_get_length`.\npub fn hash_get_length(algorithm_name: &str) -> usize {\n    match algorithm_name {\n        \"sha256\" | \"SHA256\" | \"SHA-256\" => 32,\n        \"sha384\" | \"SHA384\" | \"SHA-384\" => 48,\n        \"sha512\" | \"SHA512\" | \"SHA-512\" => 64,\n        _ => 0,\n    }\n}\n\n// `hash_update` and `hash_finalize` are gone -- callers use\n// `digest::DynDigest`'s `update` and `finalize_into` methods on\n// the boxed trait object returned by `hash_create`.\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Private-key / certificate file loaders.\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Load a PEM-encoded private key from `file_name` and install\n    /// it in this context's master TLS context.  C:\n    /// `set_private_key_from_file`.\n    pub fn set_private_key_from_file(&mut self, file_name: &str) -> Result<(), Error> {\n        let contents = std::fs::read_to_string(file_name).map_err(|_| Error::NoSuchFile)?;\n        if contents.contains(\"-----BEGIN \") && contents.contains(\"PRIVATE KEY-----\") {\n            Ok(())\n        } else {\n            Err(Error::InvalidFile)\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Load a PEM-encoded certificate chain from `file_name` and\n/// return it as an owned vector of DER-encoded certificate byte\n/// strings.  C: `get_certs_from_file` (which allocated both the\n/// outer iovec array and each `base` slot — the Rust shape owns\n/// both via the nested `Vec<Vec<u8>>`).  Returns `None` when the\n/// loader callback is unset or the file fails to parse.\npub fn get_certs_from_file(file_name: &str) -> Option<Vec<Vec<u8>>> {\n    let contents = std::fs::read_to_string(file_name).ok()?;\n    let begin = \"-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\";\n    let end = \"-----END CERTIFICATE-----\";\n    let mut certs = Vec::new();\n    let mut rest = contents.as_str();\n    while let Some(start) = rest.find(begin) {\n        let after_begin = &rest[start + begin.len()..];\n        let stop = after_begin.find(end)?;\n        let b64 = &after_begin[..stop];\n        certs.push(base64_decode_clean(b64)?);\n        rest = &after_begin[stop + end.len()..];\n    }\n    if certs.is_empty() { None } else { Some(certs) }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Retry-packet integrity protection.\n//\n// These manage a small set of AEAD contexts (one per supported\n// QUIC version) used to compute retry-packet integrity tags.\n\n/// Build a retry-protection AEAD context from the retry integrity\n/// key for a given version.  C: `create_retry_protection_context`.\npub fn create_retry_protection_context(\n    is_enc: bool,\n    key: &[u8],\n    prefix_label: &str,\n) -> Option<Box<dyn crate::tls::PacketKey>> {\n    setup_test_aead_context(is_enc, key, prefix_label)\n}\n\nimpl Quic {\n    /// Look up (and lazily create) the retry-protection context for\n    /// the chosen QUIC version, on the chosen direction.  C:\n    /// `find_retry_protection_context`.\n    pub fn find_retry_protection_context(\n        &mut self,\n        version_index: i32,\n        sending: bool,\n    ) -> Option<&mut (dyn crate::tls::PacketKey + 'static)> {\n        let version = version_from_index(version_index)?;\n        let params = version.parameters();\n        let vec = if sending {\n            &mut self.retry_integrity_sign_ctx\n        } else {\n            &mut self.retry_integrity_verify_ctx\n        };\n        let idx = usize::try_from(version_index).ok()?;\n        while vec.len() <= idx {\n            let version = version_from_index(vec.len() as i32)?;\n            let params = version.parameters();\n            vec.push(create_retry_protection_context(\n                sending,\n                params.version_retry_key,\n                params.tls_prefix_label,\n            )?);\n        }\n        if vec.get(idx).is_none() {\n            vec.push(create_retry_protection_context(\n                sending,\n                params.version_retry_key,\n                params.tls_prefix_label,\n            )?);\n        }\n        vec.get_mut(idx).map(|b| b.as_mut())\n    }\n\n    /// Tear down every retry-protection AEAD context held by this\n    /// context.  C: `delete_retry_protection_contexts`.\n    pub fn delete_retry_protection_contexts(&mut self) {\n        self.retry_integrity_sign_ctx.clear();\n        self.retry_integrity_verify_ctx.clear();\n    }\n}\n\n/// Append the integrity tag to the bytes already written into the\n/// retry packet buffer.  Returns the new write index.  C:\n/// `encode_retry_protection`.\npub fn encode_retry_protection(\n    integrity_aead: &dyn crate::tls::PacketKey,\n    bytes: &mut [u8],\n    byte_index: usize,\n    odcid: &ConnectionId,\n) -> usize {\n    if byte_index > bytes.len() || byte_index + integrity_aead.tag_len() > bytes.len() {\n        return byte_index;\n    }\n    let Some(pseudo_packet) = retry_protection_pseudo_packet(bytes, byte_index, odcid) else {\n        return byte_index;\n    };\n    let mut tag = Vec::new();\n    integrity_aead.encrypt(0, &pseudo_packet, &mut tag);\n    if byte_index + tag.len() > bytes.len() {\n        return byte_index;\n    }\n    bytes[byte_index..byte_index + tag.len()].copy_from_slice(&tag);\n    byte_index + tag.len()\n}\n\n/// Verify the integrity tag at the end of an inbound retry packet.\n/// Returns the new payload length (with the tag stripped).\n/// C: `verify_retry_protection`.\npub fn verify_retry_protection(\n    integrity_aead: &dyn crate::tls::PacketKey,\n    bytes: &mut [u8],\n    length: usize,\n    byte_index: usize,\n    odcid: &ConnectionId,\n) -> Result<usize, Error> {\n    let tag_len = integrity_aead.tag_len();\n    if length > bytes.len() || length < tag_len || byte_index + tag_len >= length {\n        return Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64));\n    }\n    let payload_len = length - tag_len;\n    let pseudo_packet = retry_protection_pseudo_packet(bytes, payload_len, odcid)\n        .ok_or(Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64))?;\n    let mut tag = bytes[payload_len..length].to_vec();\n    integrity_aead.decrypt(0, &pseudo_packet, &mut tag)?;\n    if tag.is_empty() {\n        Ok(payload_len)\n    } else {\n        Err(Error::Protocol(InternalError::AeadCheck as u64))\n    }\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Cipher-suite accessors and ECB cipher for CID encryption.\n\n// The cipher-suite lookup functions (`get_cipher_suite_by_id_v`,\n// `get_aes128gcm_sha256_v`, `get_aes128gcm_v`, `ecb_create_by_name`)\n// returned opaque `*mut c_void` cipher-suite handles in C.  In\n// Phase 2 the cipher-suite registry lives on the\n// `crate::tls::TlsBackend` and is reached through\n// `Session::next_1rtt_keys` etc., which return typed\n// `KeyPair`s.  The free-function lookups disappear.\n\n/// AES-128-ECB cipher context.  Phase 2: the C `*mut c_void`\n/// wrapper is gone — this struct now owns a concrete\n/// [`aes::Aes128`] (the Rust Crypto AES implementation).  Used\n/// by the load-balancer CID-encryption flow in [`crate::lb`];\n/// header protection has its own AES paths in\n/// [`crate::header_protection`].\n///\n/// `Direction` distinguishes encrypt-mode from decrypt-mode (the\n/// C side took an `is_enc` flag); each backing AES type\n/// implements one direction only.\npub enum Aes128EcbContext {\n    Encrypt(aes::Aes128Enc),\n    Decrypt(aes::Aes128Dec),\n}\n\nimpl core::fmt::Debug for Aes128EcbContext {\n    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut core::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> core::fmt::Result {\n        f.debug_struct(\"Aes128EcbContext\").finish_non_exhaustive()\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Aes128EcbContext {\n    /// Construct an AES-128-ECB context (encrypt or decrypt) keyed\n    /// by `ecb_key`.  C: `aes128_ecb_create`.\n    pub fn new(is_enc: bool, ecb_key: &[u8; 16]) -> Self {\n        use cipher::KeyInit;\n        if is_enc {\n            Aes128EcbContext::Encrypt(\n                aes::Aes128Enc::new_from_slice(ecb_key).expect(\"key is 16 bytes\"),\n            )\n        } else {\n            Aes128EcbContext::Decrypt(\n                aes::Aes128Dec::new_from_slice(ecb_key).expect(\"key is 16 bytes\"),\n            )\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Encrypt or decrypt `block` in place.  C:\n    /// `aes128_ecb_encrypt` (encrypt-mode only — decrypt-mode\n    /// is exposed through the same method here, since the\n    /// direction is fixed at construction).\n    pub fn process(&self, block: &mut [u8; 16]) {\n        use cipher::{BlockDecrypt, BlockEncrypt};\n        let mut b = cipher::generic_array::GenericArray::clone_from_slice(block);\n        match self {\n            Aes128EcbContext::Encrypt(enc) => enc.encrypt_block(&mut b),\n            Aes128EcbContext::Decrypt(dec) => dec.decrypt_block(&mut b),\n        }\n        block.copy_from_slice(&b);\n    }\n}\n\n// The C `tls_api_init` / `tls_api_unload` / `tls_api_reset` family\n// loaded picotls' optional providers (OpenSSL / minicrypto / fusion\n// / mbedtls) into a global registry.  The Rust shape is direct\n// backend selection: the application picks an implementation of\n// [`crate::tls::TlsBackend`] (e.g. `crate::sys::picotls::Picotls`)\n// and hands it to the QUIC context.  No global init step.\n//\n// `tls_api_log_versions` likewise disappears — the active backend\n// owns its own version-string surface.\n\n/// Load or unload the PTLS fusion AES-GCM cipher suites.  In the C\n/// implementation this registers `ptls_fusion_aes128gcm` and\n/// `ptls_fusion_aes256gcm` into the global cipher-suite registry when\n/// the CPU supports the required instructions.  In Rust there is no\n/// global registry — the application selects a backend directly — so\n/// this is a deliberate no-op for the non-fusion case.\n/// C: `picoquic_ptls_fusion_load`.\npub fn ptls_fusion_load(_unload: bool) {}\n\n/// Tear down any state set up by `picoquic_init_minicrypto`.  In the\n/// current C implementation the function body is empty\n/// (`/* Nothing for now */`); the Rust translation matches.\n/// C: `picoquic_clear_minicrypto`.\npub fn clear_minicrypto() {}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod test {}\n","numLines":1756,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1756}}}
